window.BALM_SEARCH=[{"t":"Getting started","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html","x":"Balm Studio is an Online Store 2.0 theme for Shopify: every page is built from sections and blocks that you add, remove and reorder in the theme editor, without code. This guide takes you from installation to a store ready to publish."},{"t":"Install Balm Studio from the Theme Store","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#install","x":"Open the Balm Studio page on the Shopify Theme Store while logged in to your store. Select View demo store to browse Balm Studio with its content before you install it. Select Try theme to add a trial copy to your theme library, or buy the theme straight away. A trial lets you customize everything; you pay when you publish. In your admin, go to Online Store, Themes . Balm Studio is in your theme library. Select Customize to open the theme editor. When the store is ready, open the theme's ... menu in the theme library and choose Publish . Balm Studio needs no app to work. Apps that offer app blocks, such as reviews, subscriptions or bundles, plug into the product page and into most sections."},{"t":"Updating Balm Studio","p":"Getting started / Install Balm Studio from the Theme Store","u":"index.html#updates","x":"When a new version is released, your theme library shows an update notice. Shopify adds the new version to your library as a separate copy that keeps your theme editor settings and content, so you can review it before publishing. Changes made directly in the theme code are not carried over: see Custom code . What changed in each version is listed in the Changelog ."},{"t":"The Balm Studio preset","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#preset","x":"A preset is a starting style: color schemes, font pairing, corner radii, glass recipe and typography recipes. Balm Studio comes with one preset, also named Balm Studio, and your store starts from it. Look. Clean and neutral: a white scheme, a near black scheme and two violet schemes (a pale lavender and a deep violet), sentence case headings and buttons, a white frosted glass. A calm base that lets product photography lead. Fonts. Outfit 400 for headings, Inter for body text, on one fluid type scale. Layout. Pages and sections in Full width with margins (side margins of 60 px on desktop and 20 px on mobile), and small buttons. Corners. Softly rounded: buttons 12 px, cards 20 px. Every value of the preset is a starting point. Change the colors, fonts, corners, glass and typography in Theme settings ; your sections, blocks and content stay as they are."},{"t":"How the theme editor is organized","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#editor","x":"Header group : the Announcement bar and the Header, shared by every page. Template : the sections of the page you are editing. Switch page type with the menu at the top of the editor (Home page, Products, Collections and so on). Footer group : the Footer, shared by every page. Theme settings (the gear icon): colors, fonts and storewide features. See Theme settings . Most sizes and spacings have two settings, one ending in (desktop) and one ending in (mobile) , so you can tune phones without touching large screens. Spacings switch from one value to the other at 768 px wide. Text sizes are fluid: the mobile value applies on a phone 390 px wide, the desktop value from 1440 px, and the size moves smoothly in between (see Typography ). Use the device switch at the top of the editor to preview both."},{"t":"First setup, step by step","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#first-setup","x":"Logo and menu. Open the Header section. Set Logo type and upload your Logo image , then pick your main menu under Menu . Menus themselves are edited in your admin, under Content, Menus (Online Store, Navigation on older admins). The header is transparent over the first section by default and picks its colors from what lies under it: upload a white logo in Logo for dark backgrounds so it reads over dark images (see Automatic header colors ). Countries and languages. The header shows a globe with the country and language selectors as soon as there is a choice to make: two countries or regions in Settings, Markets , or two published languages in Settings, Languages . Until then it shows nothing. Country and language selectors in the Header picks which ones appear (Both by default). See Country and language selectors . Colors. In Theme settings, Colors , adjust the four color schemes of the Balm Studio preset to your brand. Every section picks one of them. Fonts, sizes and corners. Set the Heading font and Body font in Typography . To make every heading or every text of the store larger or smaller at once, move Heading scale or Body scale there rather than each section's sizes. Set the"},{"t":"Templates included","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#templates","x":"Home page, product, collection, list of collections, search, cart, blog, blog post, page, 404, password and gift card, a second product template, product.immersive (each product's own gradient under the header, see Extend the gradient under the header ), a second collection template, collection.colorful (an Aurora gradient that runs under the header, with the column selector on), plus five page templates: page.about (About), page.contact (Contact), page.faq (FAQ), page.find-us (Store locator) and page.products (Products). All of them are built from sections, so you can reshape any of them in the editor."},{"t":"Need help?","p":"Getting started","u":"index.html#help","x":"Search this documentation with the box at the top of the page, read the FAQ , or contact Balm Studio support ."},{"t":"Theme settings","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html","x":"Theme settings apply to the whole store. Open them in the theme editor with the Theme settings icon (the gear) in the left bar. The groups below follow the order of the editor, and every label is written exactly as the editor shows it. The Default column gives the theme's built in value; the Balm Studio preset, which your store starts from, replaces the colors, fonts and typography values with its own."},{"t":"Setting groups","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#groups","x":"Colors Tone Typography Layout Buttons Tiles Product badges Pre-order Quick view Cart Gift wrapping Back to top Age verifier Favicon Social media Social media sharing Breadcrumbs Search Search engines"},{"t":"Colors","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-colors","x":"Balm Studio organizes its colors in color schemes . A scheme is a set of seven colors designed to work together, and every section, popup and drawer picks one scheme with its own Color scheme setting. Edit a scheme here and every place that uses it follows. The Balm Studio preset ships two schemes. Scheme 1 is the main one, white; Scheme 2 is its contrasting partner, near black. Add as many schemes as you need with Add scheme . Background : the section background. Background gradient is optional and replaces it where set. Text : body text, headings and icons. Button / accent and Button label : the fill and the text of primary buttons. Secondary background : the second surface of the scheme, used by cards, drawers, panels, inputs and secondary buttons. Balm Studio derives a raised tone and a hairline from it, so dark schemes keep visible layers. Accent (links / highlights) : links and highlighted details. Keep the text and button colors readable on their background: aim for a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 for body text. Glass surfaces measure their own contrast and switch the label to black or white when needed, but plain surfaces use exactly the colors you set.","l":"Accent (links / highlights) | Background | Button / accent | Button label | Secondary background | Text"},{"t":"Tone","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-tone","x":"Every product carries its own color: two colors, a dark one and a light one, read from its metafields (see Metafields, Product color ). From that pair the theme works out, on the server, the six colors of a page: the light ground (Field), the dark ground (Deep), an almost white ground (Paper), the text and the two tints in between, and it checks that every text keeps a contrast of at least 4.5:1 before printing them. The page is therefore readable without JavaScript; the browser only glides from one color to the next while a section moves. Pages without a product color (the cart, a plain page, search, the 404, a product without its metafields) use the House dark color and House light color set here.","l":"House dark color | House light color"},{"t":"Typography","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-typography","x":"Two fonts drive the whole theme: the Heading font for headings and titles, and the Body font for paragraphs, forms and everything else. Both come from the Shopify font library, so they are served by Shopify and free to use on your store. The Balm Studio preset pairs Outfit 400 for headings with Inter for body text. Type sizes. Balm Studio sets its text on one fluid scale. Every size has a mobile value, reached on a screen 390 px wide, and a desktop value, reached at 1440 px. In between, the size grows in a straight line; outside that range, it holds at the nearer value. On the scale, the product title runs from 32 to 44 px, section headings from 26 to 36 px, card titles from 15 to 17 px, body text from 15 to 16 px and small text from 12 to 13 px, each level with its own line height and letter spacing. The text size settings of sections and blocks follow the same rule: the value of a setting ending in (mobile) applies at 390 px, the one ending in (desktop) at 1440 px, and the size moves smoothly between them. Their defaults sit on the scale, so a section you add matches the rest of the page. The announcement bar and the mega menu are the exceptions: they switch from one value to the","l":"Body scale | Heading case | Heading font | Heading scale | Heading style | Heading weight | Label case | Label letter spacing | Label style | Text font"},{"t":"Layout","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-layout","x":"Page width sets how wide the content of the product, collection and search pages can grow, together with the Featured collection, Product recommendations and Recently viewed sections. Standard , the default: 1400 px at most, centered. Wide : 1600 px at most. Full width with margins : the whole screen, less the side margins of the header. The page content, the breadcrumbs and the footer then line up with the logo and the icons of the header, a floating header included. Product card images are served at the size the chosen width draws them, so cards stay sharp on a wider page. Default section width is the width of every section whose Section width is Theme default , the first option of that setting and the default of each section: Page width , Full width with margins (the default) or Full width . Change it here and every section left on Theme default follows; a section set to one of the three widths keeps its own. A section's Page width option stops at the Page width chosen above. See Section width . Section side margins (desktop) , 0 to 160 px (40 px by default), and Section side margins (mobile) , 0 to 48 px (16 px by default, under 768 px wide), set the space on each side of a sec","l":"Default section width | Page width | Section side margins (desktop) | Section side margins (mobile)"},{"t":"Buttons","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-buttons","x":"One look for every button of the theme, primary and secondary: square corners, a Size (Medium is the 60 pixel button of the Balm Studio design), a Border width and a Font weight . Every button keeps a target of at least 44 pixels. The colors come from the color of the page, or from the color scheme of a section set to Color scheme.","l":"Border width | Font weight | Size"},{"t":"Tiles","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-tiles","x":"Tiles are the product cards of every product grid: collection, search, Featured collection, recommendations, recently viewed, lookbook and complementary products. Each tile sits in the Field of its product, with the cutout standing, the name and the price at the bottom and, with Show name watermark , the first line of the name set large behind the product. Product image on hover picks what the picture does when the pointer rests on the tile. Sizes are set per device.","l":"Price size (desktop) | Price size (mobile) | Product image on hover | Product name size (desktop) | Product name size (mobile) | Show name watermark (desktop) | Show name watermark (mobile)"},{"t":"Product badges","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-product-badges","x":"Four badges can sit on the product cards, in quick view, in Compare products and on the product page. Sale shows automatically when the compare-at price is above the price, Sold out when the product can no longer be bought. New is off by default: set New badge to Product tag and name the tag, or to Created in the last X days and set the number of days. Custom prints the product's custom.badge_label metafield, read directly. This group sets their position, shape and colors once for the whole store. A product can give its Custom badge its own colors through two optional Color metafields, custom.badge_color (background) and custom.badge_text_color (text). Left empty, the badge uses Custom background and Custom text from this group. With a background and no text color, the text turns dark or light by itself, at a contrast of at least 4.5:1. See Give one product its own badge colors . On the product page, turn on Badges on media in the Product section, or add a Badge block. Every section that shows product cards has its own Badges setting (All, Automatic only, Custom only or None) to keep some of them, or none, in that section: see Choose the badges of each section . See Product badges ","l":"New badge | Number of days (X) | Position | Sale badge text | Tag"},{"t":"Pre-order","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-pre-order","x":"Pre-order turns itself on for a variant whose quantity is tracked, whose stock is at 0 and that has Continue selling when out of stock checked. The add to cart button, the sticky add to cart bar and the quick add button then read Pre-order , or the label you type here. See Pre-order .","l":"Button label"},{"t":"Quick view","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-quick-view","x":"Quick view opens a product in a modal from its card, so shoppers can pick a variant and add to cart without leaving the page. This group sets what the modal shows and how it looks. You turn it on per section, with the Quick view setting of the Collection, Featured collection, Search, Recently viewed and Lookbook sections. See Quick view . Content","l":"Description length | Preload on hover | Short description metafield | Show link to the product page | Show pickup availability | Show rating | Show short description | Show vendor"},{"t":"Cart","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-cart","x":"One set of settings for the cart drawer and the cart page. Cart type opens a drawer, shows a short notification or goes to the cart page. The drawer is a sheet against the edge of the screen, in the color of the last product added, with its Panel width , paddings and sizes set per device. Free shipping bar : a bar split by line with its sentence, toward the amount you type. It only shows progress: set the real rule in your admin (Settings, Shipping and delivery, or Discounts) and keep the two amounts the same. Recommendations : Complete your routine , products from Shopify's recommendations or from a list you pick, never a product already in the cart. Cart content : the order note, the discount code, the savings, the taxes and shipping note and a promotion note on each line. Checkout : accelerated checkout buttons in the drawer and on the cart page, in the colors Shopify gives them, and payment icons. Empty cart : a sentence, a button and, optionally, products from a collection. Drawer and notification Free shipping bar Recommendations Cart content Checkout Empty cart","l":"Ask about lines in this order | Bar height (desktop) | Bar height (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Card size | Cart type | Collection | Free shipping threshold | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Layout | Line density | Measure progress on | Message | Message before the threshold | Message once reached | Message when the cart is empty | Number of products | Order note label | Order note placeholder | Panel width (desktop) | Position | Product title size | Products | Products come from | Products heading | Promotion note text | Recommendation type | Shipping notice | Show a promotion note on each line | Show accelerated checkout buttons in the drawer | Show accelerated checkout buttons on the cart page | Show payment icons | Show price | Show products | Show quick add | Show recommendations | Show shipping notice | Show the discount code field | Show the free shipping bar | Show the order note | Show the taxes and shipping note | Show the total savings | Thumbnail size"},{"t":"Gift wrapping","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-gift-wrapping","x":"Adds a gift wrapping checkbox, and an optional gift message, to the cart drawer and the cart page. The wrapping is a real product you create in your admin, so its price, taxes and stock work like any other product. See Gift wrapping for the setup. Gift message Where to show it","l":"Checkbox label | Help text | Message label | Message maximum length (characters) | Offer a gift message | Offer gift wrapping | Show help text | Show in the cart drawer | Show on the cart page | Wrapping product"},{"t":"Back to top","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-back-to-top","x":"A Back to top link before the footer. It is a plain link to the top of the page, so it works without JavaScript; with JavaScript the page scrolls smoothly, and at once for visitors who ask for reduced motion.","l":"Show back to top link | Show on desktop | Show on mobile"},{"t":"Age verifier","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-age-verifier","x":"A modal that asks visitors to confirm their age before they browse the store, for brands that sell alcohol, tobacco or other age restricted products. The answer is remembered in the visitor's browser for the number of days you choose. See Age verifier . Content When the visitor declines Look","l":"Action | Background image | Confirm button | Decline button | Enable the age verifier | Heading | Link | Message | Minimum age | Preview in the theme editor | Remember the answer for | Text"},{"t":"Favicon","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-favicon","x":"The small icon shown in browser tabs and bookmarks. Upload a square image of at least 32 by 32 pixels; a PNG with a transparent background works best.","l":"Favicon"},{"t":"Social media","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-social-media","x":"The addresses of your profiles, typed once: Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X, YouTube, Pinterest, Snapchat, Threads, Tumblr, Vimeo and LinkedIn. Enter the full URL of each profile, for example https://www.instagram.com/yourbrand . Only the networks with a URL show, each with its icon, in the order of this list. A link opens in a new tab and is named for screen readers after your store, such as Balm on Instagram . The icons appear in three places: the Social media links block of the footer, the Social media links section, and the header on desktop when Show social media icons is checked in the Header section. See Social media .","l":"Facebook | Instagram | LinkedIn | Pinterest | Snapchat | Threads | TikTok | Tumblr | Vimeo | X | YouTube"},{"t":"Social media sharing","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-social-media-sharing","x":"Controls how your pages look when someone shares a link on social media or in a messaging app. Product, collection and blog post pages use their own featured image. The Fallback share image covers every other page (1200 x 630 pixels is the recommended size), and the X (Twitter) account is shown as the source of shared cards. The links to your own profiles are in Social media .","l":"Fallback share image | X (Twitter) account"},{"t":"Breadcrumbs","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-breadcrumbs","x":"A trail of links back to the home page, shown on product, collection and blog post pages. Position, separator and alignment are set here for the whole store. The Product, Collection and Article sections each have a Breadcrumbs on this page setting that shows or hides the trail on that page type only. Show the collection , on by default, adds a collection to the trail of a product page, and to the breadcrumb data search engines read: the collection the visitor came through, otherwise the collection set in the product's custom.primary_collection metafield, otherwise its first collection. See Metafields, Primary collection .","l":"Alignment | Position | Separator | Show breadcrumbs | Show the collection"},{"t":"Search","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-search","x":"Search scope decides what the storefront searches, both in the header suggestions and on the results page. Products only keeps the results page to product cards, which is also what the search filters need. Products, articles and pages adds your blog posts and pages to the results.","l":"Search scope"},{"t":"Search engines","p":"Theme settings","u":"theme-settings.html#ts-search-engines","x":"Shopify already tells search engines to treat a filtered or sorted collection URL as the plain collection URL. Internal search results pages are not covered by default, and they rarely deserve a place in Google. This setting adds a noindex instruction to them, and optionally to filtered collections too.","l":"Keep out of search results"},{"t":"Sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html","x":"Every section Balm Studio offers, with where it can be used, what it does, a typical use and its full list of settings. Add a section from the theme editor with Add section; drag it to reorder it. Settings tables are folded: open one to see every label, its values and its default."},{"t":"All sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#all-sections","x":"Balm Studio sections Hero sequence Campaign Color library A day in color Routine builder Reviews Atelier Line-up Hue finder Texture Ingredient atlas Chapters Numbers Contact Journal Journal article Footer Header and footer Announcement bar Header Footer Hero and storytelling Hero Slideshow Featured set Image Image with text Rich text Scroll-revealed text Bento Video Marquee Before and after Products and collections Featured product Featured collection Collection list Routine Lookbook Compare products Recently viewed Trust and engagement Key ingredients Key figures Multicolumn Testimonials Logo list Countdown Newsletter Newsletter popup Social media links FAQ About page Brand story hero Comparison panels Checklist banner Gallery banner Contact and stores Contact Store locator Layout, code and apps Divider Custom Liquid Apps Template sections Product Product recommendations Sticky add to cart Collection Search Collections list Cart Cart drawer Blog Article Page 404 page Password page Gift card Blocks used inside sections Theme blocks Mega menu blocks"},{"t":"Settings most sections share","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#shared-settings","x":"A handful of settings come back in almost every section. They work the same way everywhere, so they are explained once here."},{"t":"Color scheme","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#color-scheme","x":"Picks one of the schemes defined in Theme settings, Colors . The scheme paints the section background, its text and its buttons."},{"t":"Surface","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#section-background","x":"Most sections have a Surface setting that paints their background. Field, Deep and Paper follow the color of the page, so a section changes with the product it sits under: Field : the light ground of the product color. Deep : the dark version of the same color, with light text. Paper : an almost white ground tinted with the color. Color scheme : the section's color scheme instead of the product color. Image : a picture behind the section, with the color scheme for the text. Pages without a product color (the cart, a plain page, the 404) use the house pair of Theme settings, Tone ."},{"t":"Spacing, desktop and mobile","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#spacing","x":"Sizes and spacings come in pairs: a label ending in (desktop) applies from 768 px wide, one ending in (mobile) applies below. Top and bottom padding set the space inside the section, above and below its content. Text sizes are the exception: they are fluid. The (mobile) value applies on a screen 390 px wide, the (desktop) value from 1440 px, and the size moves smoothly in between, then Heading scale or Body scale multiplies it. See Theme settings, Typography . The announcement bar and the mega menu switch their text sizes at 1200 px instead, and decorative texts, such as the text behind cutouts of the Product section, keep a desktop and a mobile size off the scale."},{"t":"Section width","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#section-width","x":"Almost every section has a Section width setting, right after its color scheme. It sets how far the section's background, image or card reaches: Theme default , the first option and the default: the Default section width of Theme settings, Layout , Full width with margins unless you change it there. Sections left on Theme default all change width at once from there. Full width : from one edge of the screen to the other. Pictures and videos (Image, Image with text, Before and after, Video, Slideshow) run edge to edge with square corners; text sections keep their text to a readable width inside, and a grid, a table or a carousel keeps the side margin of a floating header, never more than the Section side margins. Full width with margins : the whole screen less the Section side margins of Theme settings, Layout, one value on desktop and one on mobile. Page width : stops at the Page width of Theme settings, Layout, with its side margin, so the section lines up with the product, collection and search pages. Inset in Full width with margins or Page width, the frame of Before and after and the slides of the Slideshow take Corner radius : Theme setting (media) , the media radius of Theme s"},{"t":"The header over a section","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#transparent-header","x":"With Header behavior set to Transparent at top (the default) or Adaptive in the Header section, the header can lie over the first section of a page, transparent, in the colors that suit what is under it. See Automatic header colors . Hero, Slideshow, Video, Products showcase and Brand story hero carry Allow transparent header . When the section is first on the page, the header lies over it and starts transparent. The extra top padding settings keep your content clear of the header only while it is transparent. Many other sections carry Header over this section , off by default: Contact, FAQ, Image, Page, Rich text, Multicolumn, Routine, Key ingredients, Key figures, Bento, Scroll-revealed text, Featured product, Before and after, Collection list, Compare products, Custom Liquid, Logo list, Blog, Blog post, 404, List of collections and Collection. Checked on the first section of the template, the section's background (color, gradient or image) runs up behind the announcement bar and the header, and its content starts under the header. The Product section has neither. In its Product gradient background mode, Extend the background under the header plays that part: see Extend the gradi"},{"t":"Text colors","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#text-colors","x":"Most recent sections have a Text colors setting. Color scheme keeps the text of the section's scheme. Auto reads the real background of the section (its color, gradient or picture) and keeps the scheme's text when it reaches a contrast of 4.5:1 there, otherwise switches to white or black, for the text, icons, lines and buttons. Pick Auto when a section background makes the scheme's text hard to read."},{"t":"Inner panel and text color","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#inner-panel","x":"The About page sections and Contact place their content on an inner panel, the layer between the background and the text: Solid uses the color and opacity you set, Glass uses the shared glass recipe, Hidden removes it. Text color left on None lets the section work out a readable color from the background and the panel; pick a color only to force one."},{"t":"Heading level","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#heading-level","x":"Search engines and screen readers expect exactly one main heading (H1) per page. Sections that often open a page (Hero, FAQ, Contact, Featured set, Store locator, Brand story hero) let you choose Main heading (H1) or a subheading level. The templates that open with one of them already set H1; keep H2 anywhere else. Product, collection, blog and page templates set their own H1."},{"t":"Text left empty","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#translated-defaults","x":"Many text settings say Leave empty to use the translated default . Left empty, they show a built in text that is already translated into every language the theme ships (English, French, German, Italian and Spanish). Typing your own text replaces it in every language, so on a multilingual store either leave these fields empty or translate your text with the Translate & Adapt app. See Translations ."},{"t":"Spam protection notice","p":"Sections / Settings most sections share","u":"sections.html#spam-notice","x":"Shopify protects the contact and newsletter forms with hCaptcha, which must be disclosed. Balm Studio prints the required sentence, with its two links, under each form, which removes the hCaptcha badge from the corner of the page. The Spam protection notice settings only change its size, color and alignment."},{"t":"Balm Studio sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#balm-studio-sections","x":"The sections of the Balm Studio demo store. Each one wears the color of the product it shows: the theme reads the two colors of the product (see Metafields, Product color ) and works out the ground, the text and the deep panels from them, with the contrast checked on the server. While a section moves from one product to the next, the whole page glides from one color to the other. Every section reads correctly without JavaScript, and visitors who ask for reduced motion see each step at once, without the glide. The captures come from the demo store, on a desktop screen and on a phone."},{"t":"Hero sequence","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-hero-sequence","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The products of the home page, one after the other, as you scroll. Each Product block is one step: the product name sits large behind the cutout, its last line in front of it, and a bar at the bottom shows the name, the type and format, the first sentence of the tagline, the price, View formula and Add to bag . Scrolling lifts and turns each product away while the next one rises, and the color of the page follows, with a short pause on each product. Scroll length per step sets how long each product stays, on desktop and on phones; Object height sets the size of the cutout; Bar surface paints the bar. Without JavaScript each product is a still screen in its own color. Hero sequence: the first product, its name in layers around the cutout. Typical use. Three to five products at the top of the home page, each with its two colors and its cutout.","l":"Bar surface | Object height (desktop) | Object height (mobile) | Scroll length per step (desktop) | Scroll length per step (mobile) | Show add to cart button | Show price"},{"t":"Block: Product","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Hero sequence","u":"sections.html#s-hero-sequence-product","x":"","l":"Product"},{"t":"Campaign","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-campaign","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A photo on one side and, on a flat panel, a short heading, a text, a link and a photo credit. Image position puts the photo left or right on desktop, above or below on phones, and Surface paints the panel in the light Paper of the page color, its Field or its Deep. The section has no animation. Campaign: the photo on the left, the text on Paper. Typical use. The story of a season or of a launch, between the hero and the products.","l":"Anchor | Button label | Credit | Heading | Image | Image position (desktop) | Image position (mobile) | Link | Minimum height (desktop) | Photo height (mobile) | Surface | Text"},{"t":"Color library","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-color-library","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One tall band per product, each in its own color with its name written upright. Opening a band, on hover, on click or with the keyboard, widens it and shows the product upright, its name, type, tagline, price and actions, and the section takes its color. On phones the bands stack as an accordion. Pick the products one by one in Products or a whole Collection (12 products at most); Band open at start chooses the first open band. Without JavaScript every band is a native disclosure and the first one is open. Color library: the third band open, the others in their colors. Typical use. The whole range at a glance on the home page, each product in its color.","l":"Anchor | Band height (desktop) | Band open at start | Collection | Heading | Open band height (mobile) | Products | Show add to cart button | Show price | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"A day in color","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-day-in-color","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A day told in steps. Each Step block has a large Time , a Label , a Product and a line on How to use it, and its Ground picks the light or deep color of that product: light in the morning, deep at night. As you scroll, the clock, the product and the color change from step to step. Without JavaScript the steps are a list, each in its own color. A day in color: the morning step on the light ground of its product. Typical use. Morning, noon and night routines, each step with the product that fits it.","l":"Anchor | Scroll length per step (desktop) | Scroll length per step (mobile) | Show add to cart button | Show price | Subheading"},{"t":"Block: Step","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / A day in color","u":"sections.html#s-day-in-color-step","x":"","l":"Ground | How to use | Label | Product | Time"},{"t":"Routine builder","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-routine-builder","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A large paragraph with up to three products set inline as small cutouts, then one column per Step block. Each step offers two or three products written as words; choosing one paints the column in that product's color and brings its cutout in. The summary adds up the real prices of the chosen products and Add the routine puts them all in the cart at once. Offer text is a line you write, for example the discount you set up in your admin; the theme computes no discount. Without JavaScript each step is a group of radio buttons in an add to cart form. Routine builder: the paragraph with its inline products. Typical use. Cleanse, treat and protect: shoppers build their routine and add it in one click.","l":"Anchor | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Inline product 1 | Inline product 2 | Inline product 3 | Offer text | Paragraph | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Step","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Routine builder","u":"sections.html#s-routine-builder-step","x":"","l":"Label | Products"},{"t":"Reviews","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-reviews","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A summary line you write, a link to all your reviews and up to three quotes set large, each with its stars, its author and a square in the color of the reviewed product, linked to it. Columns is set per device. Nothing is filled in for you: a Review block without a quote stays hidden on your store. Reviews: three quotes, each with the color of its product. Typical use. Three short reviews from real customers, under the products they mention.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Link | Show a rule above | Summary | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Review","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Reviews","u":"sections.html#s-reviews-review","x":"","l":"Author | Product | Quote | Rating"},{"t":"Atelier","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-atelier","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A wide photo, then on a Deep panel a heading and columns of text with their links, for example the address and the opening hours of your studio and how to book a visit. Photo height is set per device. Atelier: the photo, then the address and the appointments on Deep. Typical use. Where your workshop or shop is, when it is open, and how to visit.","l":"Anchor | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading | Image | Photo height (desktop) | Photo height (mobile) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Column","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Atelier","u":"sections.html#s-atelier-column","x":"","l":"Button label | Link | Text"},{"t":"Line-up","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-lineup","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Your products standing side by side on a ruler, each at its real height on the same scale. Each Product block has a Height , in millimeters, that you type. Hovering or focusing a product spreads its color behind the whole section and shows its name and height. On phones the line-up scrolls sideways and the product in the middle becomes active. Show the height range prints the shortest and tallest heights in the caption. Line-up: one tube focused, its color behind the section. Typical use. How big each product really is, for a range with several sizes.","l":"Anchor | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Caption heading | Heading | Link | Shelf height (desktop) | Shelf height (mobile) | Show price | Show the height range | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Word at rest"},{"t":"Block: Product","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Line-up","u":"sections.html#s-lineup-tube","x":"","l":"Height | Product"},{"t":"Hue finder","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-hue-finder","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Three questions, one at a time, answered with words. Each Question block has up to four answers, each pointing to the products it suits. The first question counts three times, the second twice, the third once, and the section slides toward the color of the leading product at each answer. The last screen shows the product, its reason, View formula and Add to bag . Remember the result for 30 days , off by default, keeps the result on the visitor's device and adds a link to forget it; off, nothing is saved. Hue finder: the second question, the color of the leading product behind it. Typical use. A short quiz that leads a hesitant shopper to one product.","l":"Anchor | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Note | Question label | Remember the result for 30 days | Result label | Show price | Starting color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Question","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Hue finder","u":"sections.html#s-hue-finder-question","x":"","l":"Answer 1 | Answer 2 | Answer 3 | Answer 4 | Products for answer 1 | Products for answer 2 | Products for answer 3 | Products for answer 4 | Question"},{"t":"Texture","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-texture","x":"Where Only on product templates. A trail of cream drawn across the screen as you scroll, in the color of the product, beside its Texture , its Skin feel and How to use . It belongs to the product template and reads the product of the page. Connect each text to a metafield to give every product its own (see Metafields, Product texts ); an empty text is not printed. Texture: the trail fully drawn, the texture and the skin feel beside it. Typical use. Under the product details, to show what the formula feels like.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | How to use | Show add to cart button | Show price | Skin feel | Skin feel label | Subheading | Texture | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Ingredient atlas","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-ingredient-atlas","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A wall of ingredient names. Each Ingredient block has a Name , a Note and the Products that contain it; hovering or focusing a name shows its note and the products, in their colors. The atlas reads its blocks only: there is no metaobject to create. Ingredient atlas: one ingredient focused, with the products that contain it. Typical use. The key ingredients of the range, each linked to the products that use it.","l":"Anchor | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading | Note heading | Note text | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Ingredient","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Ingredient atlas","u":"sections.html#s-ingredient-atlas-ingredient","x":"","l":"Name | Note | Products"},{"t":"Chapters","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-chapters","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A brand story in chapters. Each Chapter block has a Numeral , a Heading , a Text and can show a Product and a link; each chapter is painted in the color of its product. Tint the page with the first chapter gives the whole page that color from the start. It is the section of the About page of the demo. Chapters: the first chapter, in the color of its product. Typical use. The About page: three chapters of your story, each with the product it led to.","l":"Breadcrumbs on this page | Chapter height (desktop) | Tint the page with the first chapter"},{"t":"Block: Chapter","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Chapters","u":"sections.html#s-chapters-chapter","x":"","l":"Button label | Heading | Link | Numeral | Product | Show the product | Text"},{"t":"Numbers","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-numbers","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Large figures with a line of text under each, on Deep by default. Each Number block is one figure. Type only figures that are true for your brand. Numbers: three figures on Deep, above the footer. Typical use. Three facts about how you make your products.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Number","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Numbers","u":"sections.html#s-numbers-number","x":"","l":"Figure | Text"},{"t":"Contact","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-contact","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The contact page of the demo: a heading and a text, the contact form with underlined fields and a choice of Subjects you type one per line, and Detail blocks beside it (a label, a value and an optional link). A detail without a value is not printed. The form works without JavaScript. Contact: the form and the details, in the house color. Typical use. Your support hours, your studio address and the form, on the Contact page.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs on this page | Button label | Heading | Subject label | Subjects | Success message | Surface | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Detail","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Contact","u":"sections.html#s-main-contact-detail","x":"","l":"Label | Link | Value"},{"t":"Journal","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-journal","x":"Where Part of the blog template. The blog page as a journal: the newest article featured large, in the color of its product, then the other articles as rows. An article takes the color of the product picked in its custom.product metafield (see Metafields, Article product ). Journal: the newest article featured in the color of its product. Typical use. A blog with routines and ingredient notes, each article linked to one product.","l":"Articles per page | Breadcrumbs on this page | Feature the newest article | Read label | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Journal article","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-journal-article","x":"Where Part of the article template. The article page of the journal: a reading bar, the article in a comfortable measure, the product of the article ( custom.product ) and a link to the next article. Each part can be turned off. Journal article: the title in the color of its product. Typical use. Long reads that end on the product they talk about.","l":"Breadcrumbs on this page | Next article label | Product label | Show the article's product | Show the next article | Show the reading bar | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Footer","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections","u":"sections.html#s-tone-footer","x":"Where Footer group only. The footer of the demo: a Newsletter block with an underlined field, Links blocks that each show a menu, Text blocks, then your store name set very large, the copyright and a second legal line. It is painted on Deep by default and follows the color of the page. Footer: the newsletter, two menus and the store name. Typical use. Newsletter signup, the shop and help menus, and the legal lines.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Copyright | Mark | Second legal line | Show policy links | Show the store name mark | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Newsletter","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-tone-footer-newsletter","x":"","l":"Button label | Field placeholder | Heading | Text"},{"t":"Block: Links","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-tone-footer-links","x":"","l":"Heading | Menu"},{"t":"Block: Text","p":"Sections / Balm Studio sections / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-tone-footer-text","x":"","l":"Heading | Text"},{"t":"Header and footer","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#header-and-footer","x":"These sections live in the header and footer groups, shared by every page of the store."},{"t":"Announcement bar","p":"Sections / Header and footer","u":"sections.html#s-announcement-bar","x":"Where Header group only. A thin bar above the header, made of Message blocks. With two messages or more they rotate on their own, with optional previous and next arrows, and each message can link somewhere. With Show close button on, visitors can dismiss the bar for the rest of their visit. Display set to Scroll continuously runs the messages across the bar in a loop, like the Marquee section: Scrolling speed in pixels per second, Direction , a Separator between the messages (Dot, Dash or Custom text), Pause on hover and a pause button for visitors. Keyboard focus on a link stops the band and brings the link into view. Visitors who ask for reduced motion see the messages standing still, centred, on as many lines as they need. It works in every layout and style of the bar, Floating, Glass and Content color Auto included. Scroll behavior keeps the bar pinned, lets it scroll away with the page, or hides it on the way down and brings it back on the way up. Bar layout set to Floating turns it into a card that matches the floating header, and Bar style set to Glass uses the shared glass recipe. A floating bar sits over the first section when the header is transparent there. Use the heade","l":"Bar layout | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Corner radius (desktop) | Corner radius (mobile) | Direction | Display | Letter spacing (desktop) | Letter spacing (mobile) | Match the header corner radius | Pause on hover | Rotation delay | Scroll behavior | Scrolling speed | Separator | Separator color | Separator size | Separator text | Show a pause button | Show announcement bar | Show arrows | Show close button | Space before the header (desktop) | Space before the header (mobile) | Space between messages (desktop) | Space between messages (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top margin (desktop) | Top margin (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Use the header's colors over dark backgrounds"},{"t":"Block: Message","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Announcement bar","u":"sections.html#s-announcement-bar-message","x":"One message, with an optional link that makes the whole message clickable.","l":"Link | Message"},{"t":"Header","p":"Sections / Header and footer","u":"sections.html#s-header","x":"Where Header group only. The logo (an image, or your store name as a wordmark), the main menu, search, the account and the bag. The header takes the color of the section under it: Field, Deep, Paper or the product color, with the text checked at a 4.5:1 contrast, and it hides on the way down and comes back on the way up. A mega menu opens as an index on Deep: the categories set large with their product count, the products of the hovered category and a preview of the product, the panel following its color. On phones the menu opens as a full screen sheet on Deep. Search opens full screen, with your popular products and suggestions in words. Mega menus are built with the Mega menu blocks ."},{"t":"Header colors","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Header","u":"sections.html#s-header-tone","x":"Over a first section that allows it (see The header over a section ), the header is transparent at the top of the page. As the page scrolls it takes the surface of the section under it, Field, Deep, Paper, a color scheme or an image, with its text and the announcement bar kept readable at a 4.5:1 contrast. There is nothing to set per section."},{"t":"Country and language selectors","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Header","u":"sections.html#s-header-localization","x":"Country and language selectors shows the current country and currency in the header, for example France (EUR) ; it opens a small window with the two lists and an Update button. It uses the localization form of Shopify and works without JavaScript. Add countries and languages in your admin, under Settings, Markets and Settings, Languages . Header: the Shop mega menu, an index of categories on Deep. Header on a phone: the menu sheet on Deep. Typical use. Your logo as a wordmark, the Shop menu as an index of categories, search and the bag. Logo Navigation Mobile menu Product menu Actions Search Layout Header Colors This section holds Mega menu blocks .","l":"Color scheme | Colors over dark backgrounds | Country and language selectors | Customer account menu | Enable predictive search | Floating corner radius (desktop) | Floating corner radius (mobile) | Floating header (detached) | Floating side margins (desktop) | Floating side margins (mobile) | Floating top margin (desktop) | Floating top margin (mobile) | Follow the global corner radius | Header behavior | Header vertical padding (desktop) | Header vertical padding (mobile) | Logo for dark backgrounds | Logo image | Logo link | Logo text | Logo type | Logo width (desktop) | Logo width (mobile) | Max thumbnail width (desktop) | Mega menu alignment (desktop) | Mega menu color scheme | Menu | No results hint | Panel corner radius (desktop) | Panel corner radius (mobile) | Popular products | Results per resource type | Search placeholder | Search suggestions | Secondary links | Show a background behind the thumbnail | Show cart | Show collections in results | Show product tagline | Show social media icons | Sticky header | Thumbnail background color | Thumbnail size | Wordmark size (desktop) | Wordmark size (mobile)"},{"t":"Footer","p":"Sections / Header and footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer","x":"Where Footer group only. The footer is a row of blocks: Large logo , Brand / logo , Link column (one of your menus), Newsletter , Social media links (the icons of your profiles and the Follow on Shop button), Text and Localization (country or currency, and language selectors, shown only when there is more than one choice). Each block sets its own width and margins for desktop and mobile. The Large logo always takes a row of its own, wherever it sits among the blocks. Under Typography , Column heading size and Link size each have a desktop and a mobile value (14 and 13 px by default). They are fluid like every text size of the theme: the desktop value applies from 1440 px wide and moves toward the mobile value on narrower screens. An optional Top decorative band draws a curve, a wave, a diagonal or your own image where the footer meets the section above. The Copyright bar at the bottom can take its own color scheme. Newsletter sign ups are added to your Shopify customers, with the tag you choose. Typical use. The store name as a large wordmark across the footer, then the logo and tagline, Shop and Help link columns, a newsletter block, and a localization block for a store that sells","l":"Block distribution (desktop) | Block distribution (mobile) | Color scheme | Column heading size (desktop) | Column heading size (mobile) | Copyright bar color scheme | Copyright bar colors | Copyright text | Horizontal spacing between blocks | Link size (desktop) | Link size (mobile) | Padding bottom (desktop) | Padding bottom (mobile) | Padding top (desktop) | Padding top (mobile) | Show copyright bar at bottom | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Large logo","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-large-logo","x":"A large logo across the whole footer, on a row of its own. It comes first in the footer the theme ships with, and one footer holds one Large logo. Text , the default, sets the store name, or the Text you type, in the heading font, with the case, weight and style of Theme settings, Typography. The size is worked out so the letters fill the width on one line, and follows the width as the screen changes. Image takes your own artwork. Use an SVG, served as it is, or a transparent PNG at least 3000 px wide, so the logo stays sharp across a large screen; a PNG or JPG is served up to 3840 px wide. Recolor SVG draws a single color SVG in the color you choose; other images keep their own colors. Fill Alt text only when the header logo does not already give the store name: left empty, screen readers skip the image. Width lines the logo up with the footer columns (Content width) or runs it from one edge of the screen to the other (Full width). Alignment only has an effect when the logo is narrower than the row, which a fitted text or an image at full width never is. Crop bottom hides up to half of the logo's height, so it looks cut off by the edge of the footer. Color takes the text color of ","l":"Alignment | Alt text | Color | Crop bottom | Custom color | Logo image | Logo type | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Opacity | Recolor SVG | Show on mobile | Text | Width"},{"t":"Block: Brand / logo","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-brand","x":"Your logo, or the store name when no logo is set, with an optional tagline. Spacing","l":"Logo image | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Tagline (optional) | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Link column","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-link-column","x":"A heading and one of your menus. Spacing","l":"Header | Heading spacing (desktop) | Heading spacing (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Menu | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Newsletter","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-newsletter","x":"An email sign up field. Subscribers are added to your customers with the tag you set, which email apps such as Klaviyo or Mailchimp can read. Spam protection notice Email field Spacing","l":"Customer tag for subscribers | Field maximum width (desktop) | Field maximum width (mobile) | Heading spacing (desktop) | Heading spacing (mobile) | Input placeholder | Label | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Minimum column width (desktop) | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Social media links","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-social","x":"The icons of the profiles typed in Theme settings, Social media , only the networks with a URL, and the Follow on Shop button, which Shopify shows only on stores that use the Shop sales channel. Spacing","l":"Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Show the Follow on Shop button | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Text","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-text","x":"A heading and rich text, for an address or a short note. Spacing","l":"Body | Heading | Heading spacing (desktop) | Heading spacing (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Localization","p":"Sections / Header and footer / Footer","u":"sections.html#s-footer-localization","x":"Country or currency, and language selectors. Each appears only when your markets and languages offer more than one choice. Spacing","l":"Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Show country / currency selector | Show language selector | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Hero and storytelling","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#hero-and-storytelling","x":"Large visual sections, usually at the top of the home page or of a landing page."},{"t":"Hero","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-hero","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A full screen image or Shopify hosted video with a title and a button. Desktop and mobile each get their own image and video, cropped on the focal point you set in the admin. Video playback covers autoplay per device, a sound button, what happens at the end (loop, stop, or show the cover again), and the style and position of the controls. The cover always paints first, the video fades in over it, and the controls appear with the video, never before it. While the video loads has two styles. Cover image, then fade , the default, shows the cover sharp until the video plays. Blurred cover, then fade keeps the cover blurred until then. The hero has no loader of its own: for a loading screen, turn on the Page loader in Theme settings, Loader. A hero set to a loader style in a preview version of Balm Studio now shows Cover image, then fade. The text block is placed separately on desktop and mobile, with a fine vertical offset, over an optional darkening overlay. Height mode (desktop) and Height mode (mobile) fit the screen, adapt to the content or take a custom height. Typical use. The first section of the home page: a short","l":"Allow transparent header | Autoplay (desktop) | Autoplay (mobile) | Button background (hover) | Button label | Button link | Button text color (hover) | Color scheme | Controls position (desktop) | Controls position (mobile) | Controls style (desktop) | Controls style (mobile) | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Eyebrow | Fine vertical offset | Heading | Heading level | Height mode (desktop) | Height mode (mobile) | Hero image (mobile) | Hero image (overrides bundled default) | Horizontal alignment | Media type | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Section width | Shopify-hosted video | Shopify-hosted video (mobile) | Sound | Subheading | Surface | Transparent header top padding (desktop) | Transparent header top padding (mobile) | Vertical position | When the video ends | While the video loads"},{"t":"Slideshow","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-slideshow","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A carousel of Slide blocks. Each slide has its own desktop and mobile image, color scheme and overlay, a heading and subtext placed in one of nine positions, and up to two buttons in Solid, Outline or Glass style. Slides change on their own or on demand, with a slide or fade transition, arrows and dots. In Full width the slides run edge to edge with square corners. In Full width with margins or Page width they are inset and take Corner radius : Theme setting (media) by default, or Custom with Custom corner radius (desktop) and (mobile) , 0 to 40 px, square at 0. The radius cuts the image, the overlay and every layer of the slide. Typical use. Two to four campaigns at the top of the home page: a new product, a seasonal collection and a bundle offer. Section background More settings More settings Height Behavior Transparent header Spacing","l":"Allow transparent header | Autoplay | Autoplay delay | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Carousel accessibility label | Color scheme | Corner radius | Custom corner radius (desktop) | Custom corner radius (mobile) | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Section width | Show arrows (desktop) | Show arrows (mobile) | Show dots | Slide height (desktop) | Slide height (mobile) | Space under a transparent header (desktop) | Space under a transparent header (mobile) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Transition"},{"t":"Block: Slide","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Slideshow","u":"sections.html#s-slideshow-slide","x":"One slide: images, overlay, heading, subtext, content position and up to two buttons. Content Buttons","l":"Background color | Color scheme | Content position | First button label | First button link | First button style | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image (desktop) | Image (mobile) | Image fit (desktop) | Image fit (mobile) | Image position (desktop) | Image position (mobile) | Image size (desktop) | Image size (mobile) | Overlay opacity | Second button label | Second button link | Second button style | Subtext"},{"t":"Featured set","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-featured-set","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One product, usually a bundle or a discovery set, presented as a full width banner: a heading, a tagline in two parts and an add to cart button. Pick the Product and the section fills itself: its title as the heading, its custom.tagline metafield as the tagline, its custom.background_color metafield as the background, and its image. The button adds that product to the cart. Each field of the Override (optional) group replaces one of those values: leave a field empty to use the product's value, and a background that neither gives takes the color scheme's. Tagline, second part has no product value: it shows only what you type. Your own desktop and mobile background images replace the product image, darkened by an optional overlay. Until a product is picked, the section shows a placeholder in the editor and nothing on the storefront. See Metafields . Typical use. Promoting a discovery set at the top of the Products page template (page.products), which opens with this section. Override (optional) Text Colors This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background color | Background image | Background image (mobile) | Button label | Color scheme | Heading | Heading level | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Product | Section width | Show the product image | Tagline | Tagline, second part"},{"t":"Image","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-image","x":"Where Only on * templates. One picture, with an optional Image (mobile) shown under 768 px. Each picture shows at its own focal point, and a phone downloads only its own. Ratio (desktop) and Ratio (mobile) keep the picture's own shape (Original) or set one (1:1, 4:5, 3:2, 16:9, 21:9 or a custom height), with Fit to fill or contain. A link, a corner radius, a border, an overlay and a Scroll animation (Fade in, Zoom out or Parallax, never for visitors who ask for reduced motion) complete it. Visibility shows it on both devices, desktop only or mobile only. Add a Caption block for a line of text under the picture. As the first section of a page, the picture loads at once, with a high priority. With Section width on Full width and Header over this section checked, the header lies over the picture and reads its tone. Typical use. A wide lifestyle photo between two sections of the home page, or a campaign visual at the top of a landing page, with a lighter crop for phones. Media Layout Style Animation and visibility Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Border width | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Header over this section | Image | Image (mobile) | Link | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Ratio (desktop) | Ratio (mobile) | Reveal on scroll | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Visibility"},{"t":"Block: Caption","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Image","u":"sections.html#s-image-caption","x":"A short text under the picture, with its size per device, its alignment and its spacing. Text color left empty takes a color that reads on the section background.","l":"Alignment | Text | Text color | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text top spacing (desktop) | Text top spacing (mobile)"},{"t":"Image with text","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-image-with-text","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An image beside a content column you build from theme blocks : headings, text, buttons, images, spacers and custom Liquid. Choose the image side on desktop, the order on mobile, the image width and ratio, and the gap. Translucent card (glass) lets the content card overlap the image on desktop. Typical use. Telling the brand story or explaining one product benefit, with a photo, a heading, two short paragraphs and a button. Layout Image Content Section background More settings More settings This section accepts the theme blocks (Heading, Text, Button, Image, Spacer, Liquid).","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content inner padding (desktop) | Content inner padding (mobile) | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Image | Image / text gap (desktop) | Image / text gap (mobile) | Image position (desktop) | Image width (desktop) | Minimum height (desktop) | Minimum height (mobile) | Order (mobile) | Ratio | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Rich text","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-rich-text","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A single column of theme blocks (headings, text, buttons, images, spacers, custom Liquid) in a narrow, normal or wide measure, aligned separately on desktop and mobile. Background set to Transparent lets the section sit on the page without its own fill. Typical use. A brand statement between two visual sections, or an introduction paragraph at the top of a landing page. Section background More settings More settings This section accepts the theme blocks (Heading, Text, Button, Image, Spacer, Liquid).","l":"Background | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content alignment (desktop) | Content alignment (mobile) | Content width | Header over this section | Inner padding (desktop) | Inner padding (mobile) | Section width | Style | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Scroll-revealed text","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-scroll-text","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One strong statement whose words light up one after another as it scrolls into view. Type it in Text ; a line break starts a new paragraph, and words between asterisks, *like this* , are highlighted in the Highlight style you pick: Italic, Accent color or Underline. Strength of unread words sets how faint the words are before they light up; it is raised automatically when needed, so they always keep a contrast of 3:1 with the background. Visitors who ask for reduced motion, and browsers without scroll animations, see every word lit at once. Typical use. The brand promise in two short sentences between the hero and the products, with two key words highlighted. Heading and intro Text Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Alignment | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Highlight style | Intro | Section width | Strength of unread words | Surface | Text | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Bento","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-bento","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A grid of tiles of different sizes: four columns on desktop, two on phones. Add Image tile , Text tile , Product tile , Stat tile and Video tile blocks, and give each a Size (desktop) and a Size (mobile) of one or two columns and one or two rows. Order on mobile moves a tile forward on phones without changing the desktop order. Row height , Card gap and Corner radius set the grid; rows grow when a tile, such as a product card, needs more room. Typical use. A home page block that mixes a large lifestyle photo, a best seller, a key figure such as 98% natural origin and a short brand text. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Intro | Row height (desktop) | Row height (mobile) | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Image tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-image","x":"A picture with an optional heading over it, in white over a dark gradient, and an optional link. Size and order","l":"Heading | Image | Link | Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Text tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-text","x":"A heading, a text and an optional button, on a color scheme of its own (Scheme 2 by default). Size and order","l":"Button label | Button link | Color scheme | Heading | Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text"},{"t":"Block: Product tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-product","x":"A product card, with its own Badges setting (All, Automatic only, Custom only or None). Size and order","l":"Badges | Order on mobile | Product | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Stat tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-stat","x":"A large number and its label, on a color scheme of its own. Size and order","l":"Color scheme | Label | Number | Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Video tile","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling / Bento","u":"sections.html#s-bento-video","x":"A video uploaded to Shopify. It plays muted, with its controls, only when the visitor starts it. Size and order","l":"Order on mobile | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Video"},{"t":"Video","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-video","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A video from Shopify (uploaded in the admin) or from YouTube or Vimeo, with its own mobile source. External videos load as a click to play cover: nothing from the third party loads before the click. Shopify videos can instead play muted on a loop with no controls. Choose the aspect ratio, full width or a maximum width, and an optional heading. Typical use. A one minute brand film on the About page, or a muted loop of the product being prepared on the home page. Section background More settings Content Video source Layout Spacing Transparent header","l":"Allow transparent header | Aspect ratio | Autoplay muted loop (Shopify video only) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Custom cover image | External video URL | External video URL (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Maximum width (desktop) | Section width | Shopify-hosted video | Shopify-hosted video (mobile) | Space under a transparent header (desktop) | Space under a transparent header (mobile) | Start with sound | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Marquee","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-marquee","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A band of text that scrolls across the screen. Type one message per line; the separator you pick (a dot, a dash, your own text or a small image) is inserted between them automatically. Set the speed, the direction and the height, and keep the pause button on: accessibility guidelines ask for one on any animation that runs by itself. Typical use. Short claims between two sections, such as Free delivery from 40 euros, Vegan, Made in France. Separator Section background More settings More settings Size Spacing","l":"Animation speed (seconds per cycle) | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Direction | Font size (desktop) | Font size (mobile) | Height (desktop) | Height (mobile) | Messages | Section width | Separator | Separator image | Separator image height (desktop) | Separator image height (mobile) | Separator text | Show a pause button | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Before and after","p":"Sections / Hero and storytelling","u":"sections.html#s-before-after","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Two images stacked on top of each other with a handle the visitor drags to compare them, horizontally or vertically. Add labels, a starting position, a round handle or a plain line, a heading and text. The handle also works from the keyboard, through a slider. In Full width the frame runs edge to edge with square corners. In Full width with margins or Page width it is inset and takes Corner radius : Theme setting (media) by default, or Custom with Custom corner radius , 0 to 40 px. See Section width . Typical use. Showing the result of a product: a surface before and after cleaning, skin before and after four weeks, a room before and after. Content Images Comparison Layout Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"After image | After image (mobile) | After label | Background image (mobile) | Before image | Before image (mobile) | Before label | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content alignment | Header over this section | Heading | Image ratio | Image ratio (mobile) | Orientation | Section width | Starting position | Surface | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Products and collections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#products-and-collections","x":"Sections that show products or collections and let shoppers buy from them."},{"t":"Featured product","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-featured-product","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. One product, picked in Product , presented on any page with the blocks of the product page: title, price, variant picker, Buy buttons with the quantity and Buy it now, description, collapsible rows and the others, plus the theme blocks and app blocks. Its media show in a gallery: images, Shopify hosted videos, YouTube and Vimeo videos and 3D models with the AR button, with the gallery arrows of Theme settings, Carousels . Choosing a variant updates the price and shows the variant's image, without changing the page address. Add to cart opens the cart as Theme settings, Cart says. Without a product, the theme editor shows a placeholder and nothing shows on the storefront. Typical use. Launching a new product on the home page, with its gallery, its variant picker and Add to cart, two sections under the hero. Scene Media Section background More settings More settings Spacing This section accepts the theme blocks (Heading, Text, Button, Image, Spacer, Liquid) and accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Gallery arrows | Header over this section | Media controls style | Media position (desktop) | Media ratio | Order (mobile) | Product | Scene height (mobile) | Scene width (desktop) | Section width | Show the AR button on 3D models | Sticky scene (desktop) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Featured collection","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-featured-collection","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A grid of products from one collection, with the full product card: second image on hover, quick add, quick view, badges, vendor and a button. Promo tile blocks take the place of a card at the position you choose, and a View all button can link to the collection. Typical use. Best sellers on the home page: four products, quick add on, a promo tile in third position and a View all button. Section background More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Card button View all button Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button alignment | Button horizontal padding (desktop) | Button horizontal padding (mobile) | Button label | Button style | Button text size (desktop) | Button text size (mobile) | Button vertical padding (desktop) | Button vertical padding (mobile) | Card button label | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Collection | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Element order | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image fit | Image ratio | Layout on desktop | Layout on mobile | Maximum products | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Second image on hover | Section width | Show the \"View all\" button | Show vendor | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Promo tile","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Featured collection","u":"sections.html#s-featured-collection-promo-tile","x":"A tile that takes the place of a product card at the position you choose, on the first page of the grid only.","l":"Button label | Color scheme | Heading | Image | Image (mobile) | Link | Position in the grid | Text | Text alignment | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Collection list","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-collection-list","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Cards for the collections you pick with Collection blocks, with their image, title and an optional product count. Set the columns, the gap, the image ratio and fit. Typical use. A Shop by category row on the home page with three or four collections. Section background More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Layout on desktop | Layout on mobile | Section width | Show product count | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Collection","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Collection list","u":"sections.html#s-collection-list-collection","x":"One collection card.","l":"Collection"},{"t":"Routine","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-routine","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A care routine, step by step. Each Step block holds a step label, a product, a short text and a moment: Morning, Evening, or both. With Show Morning and Evening tabs , two tabs show the steps of one moment at a time; they appear only when at least one step is for a single moment. Show the total price adds the price of the moment's products, and the button adds them all to the cart in one go, then opens the cart as Theme settings, Cart says. It works without JavaScript too. Columns and Card style set the layout. Second image on hover crossfades to the step's Image on hover , or to the product's second image. Typical use. A Morning and evening routine of four products (cleanser, serum, cream and night balm) on a product page or the home page, with Add the routine. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Intro | Second image on hover | Section width | Show Morning and Evening tabs | Show the total price | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Step","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Routine","u":"sections.html#s-routine-step","x":"One step of the routine: a Step label (the number of the step when empty), a product, an optional Image that replaces the product's, a short text and its Moment : Morning and evening, Morning or Evening.","l":"Image | Image on hover | Moment | Product | Step label | Text"},{"t":"Lookbook","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-lookbook","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. An image with Hotspot blocks. Each hotspot points at a product or shows a text; on desktop it opens a popover with the product card and its quick add, on a phone a sheet from the bottom of the screen. The Image with product list layout lines the products up as cards beside the image, and hovering a card lights its hotspot. Hotspots have separate desktop and mobile positions. Typical use. Shop the look: a styled photo of three products used together, each one clickable and addable to the cart. Section background More settings More settings Content Image Layout Hotspots Product cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card image ratio | Color scheme | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Hotspot color | Hotspot colors | Hotspot icon | Hotspot icon color | Hotspot size (desktop) | Hotspot size (mobile) | Image | Image (mobile) | Image ratio | Layout | Product list position | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Section width | Surface | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Hotspot","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Lookbook","u":"sections.html#s-lookbook-hotspot","x":"One point on the image, linked to a product or carrying a text, with its desktop and mobile position. Position (desktop) Position (mobile)","l":"Content | Heading | Horizontal position | Link | Link label | Product | Text | Vertical position"},{"t":"Compare products","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-compare-products","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. Up to five products side by side. Built in rows show the image, the badges, the price, the availability, the vendor and the rating. Each Row block adds a line: its Label sits in the left column, and its value is read on every compared product from its Source : Metafield, Vendor, Product type, Tags, SKU, Barcode, Weight or Unit price. With Metafield, type the metafield's name as in your admin (Skin type) or its key (custom.skin_type) in Metafield . Each value is drawn by its type: yes and no as icons, a list as a sentence, a number with the row's Unit , a color with its swatch, a reference by its title. Highlight differences marks the rows where products differ, and an empty value shows a hyphen. Mobile layout shows one card per product (Cards), or keeps the table with the label column in place while the product columns scroll (Scroll). See Metafields, Compare products rows for an example. Typical use. Comparing the three creams of a range on their key facts: texture, skin type and whether they are fragrance free. Section background More settings More settings Content Rows Product cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Column width (mobile) | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Highlight differences | Mobile layout | Products | Quick add | Quick add label | Section width | Show availability | Show price | Show product image | Show rating | Show vendor | Surface | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Row","p":"Sections / Products and collections / Compare products","u":"sections.html#s-compare-products-row","x":"One comparison line: a Label , and a Source read on every compared product (a metafield by its name or key, the vendor, the product type, the tags, the SKU, the barcode, the weight or the unit price). See Metafields .","l":"Label | Metafield | Source | Unit"},{"t":"Recently viewed","p":"Sections / Products and collections","u":"sections.html#s-recently-viewed","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. The products the visitor opened most recently, newest first. The list is kept in the visitor's own browser, so it needs no app and no account; the section takes no space until there is a history. The theme editor shows example cards instead. Typical use. At the bottom of product pages, with the current product excluded, or on the cart page. Section background More settings More settings Content Layout Cards Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Exclude the current product | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Maximum products | Mobile layout | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Trust and engagement","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#trust-and-engagement","x":"Reassurance, proof, social proof and ways to stay in touch."},{"t":"Key ingredients","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-key-ingredients","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The ingredients that make a product work, one Ingredient block each: a picture, a name, the benefit it brings and a detail. Layout (desktop) and Layout (mobile) show them as a grid, a carousel, or Auto, a carousel only when the cards outnumber the columns. The carousel uses the arrows of Theme settings, Carousels . Detail set to Over the picture shows the detail on the picture on hover or focus with a mouse, and through each ingredient's More about button on every device; set to Always under the benefit, it is always visible. Turn off Show button in an ingredient to remove its button. Image ratio takes a square, portrait, landscape or circle frame. Typical use. Three hero ingredients of a serum, each with a close up photo, the benefit in one line and where it comes from. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Carousel navigation | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Detail | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image ratio | Intro | Layout (desktop) | Layout (mobile) | Next card preview (mobile) | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Ingredient","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Key ingredients","u":"sections.html#s-key-ingredients-ingredient","x":"One ingredient: a picture, a name, the benefit and a detail. With Show button , a More about button reveals the detail; fill Button link to make it open a page instead.","l":"Benefit | Button label | Button link | Detail | Image | Name | Show button"},{"t":"Key figures","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-key-figures","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A row of figures, one Figure block each: a number with an optional prefix and suffix, a label and a source note. Count up the numbers counts each figure up once when it scrolls into view; it works on plain numbers, such as 98 or 4.8, and never for visitors who ask for reduced motion. The real figure is always in the page for screen readers. Columns, gaps, alignment, number sizes and Card style (None, Solid, Outline or Glass) set the look. Only state figures you can prove, and say where each one comes from in its Source note . Typical use. Results of a consumer test under a product launch: 98% feel softer skin, 4.8 out of 5 average rating, 30 days of use, with the study named in the source notes. Heading and intro Layout Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Alignment | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Count up the numbers | Header over this section | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Intro | Number size (desktop) | Number size (mobile) | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Figure","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Key figures","u":"sections.html#s-key-figures-figure","x":"One figure: the Number , an optional Prefix and Suffix (keep the unit there, so the number counts up), a Label that says what it measures and an optional Source note .","l":"Label | Number | Prefix | Source note | Suffix"},{"t":"Multicolumn","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-multicolumn","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A row of Column blocks, each with an image (square, landscape, portrait or circle), a heading, text and a link, plus an optional button for the whole section. On phones the columns stack or become a horizontal slider. Typical use. Three reasons to buy, or How it works in three steps, each with a small illustration. Section background More settings More settings Content Layout Section button Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Color scheme | Column gap (desktop) | Column gap (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Content alignment | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Icon size | Icon style | Mobile layout | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Column","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Multicolumn","u":"sections.html#s-multicolumn-column","x":"One column: image, heading, text and link.","l":"Heading | Icon | Image | Image ratio | Image width (desktop) | Image width (mobile) | Link | Link label | Text"},{"t":"Testimonials","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-testimonials","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Testimonial blocks with a quote, a star rating, an author, a role or source and an avatar, as a grid or a horizontal slider. The slider can rotate on its own; it pauses on hover and focus and stops for good once the visitor takes control. Cards are Solid, Outline or Glass. Typical use. Five short customer quotes in a slider under the product showcase, or press quotes with the name of the publication as the source. Section background More settings More settings Content Layout Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card background | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card style | Cards visible (desktop) | Change every | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Desktop layout | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Mobile layout | Rotate automatically | Section width | Show arrows (desktop) | Show arrows (mobile) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Testimonial","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Testimonials","u":"sections.html#s-testimonials-testimonial","x":"One testimonial card.","l":"Author | Avatar | Quote | Role or source | Star rating (0 hides stars)"},{"t":"Logo list","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-logo-list","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A row of Logo blocks with an optional heading, shown still or scrolling as a marquee. Logos can be grayscale until hovered and can each link somewhere. Typical use. An As seen in row of press logos, or the retailers that stock your products. Section background More settings More settings Content Logos Spacing","l":"Alignment | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Case | Color scheme | Gap (desktop) | Gap (mobile) | Header over this section | Heading | Logo height (desktop) | Logo height (mobile) | Section width | Show logos in the text color | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Space below heading (desktop) | Space below heading (mobile) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Weight"},{"t":"Block: Logo","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / Logo list","u":"sections.html#s-logo-list-logo","x":"One logo, with an optional link.","l":"Link | Logo image"},{"t":"Countdown","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-countdown","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A timer counting down to a date and time in your store's timezone (format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM ), with days, hours, minutes and seconds you can show or hide and rename. When it reaches zero it shows a message or hides the section. Typical use. The last days of a sale, or the launch of a limited edition. Section background More settings Content Target Units Style Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Days label | Digit size (desktop) | Digit size (mobile) | End message | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Hours label | Minutes label | Seconds label | Section width | Show days | Show hours | Show minutes | Show seconds | Subtext | Surface | Target date | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Unit box style | When the countdown ends"},{"t":"Newsletter","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-newsletter","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An email sign up band with a heading and subtext, on a solid or glass panel or on no panel at all, over the section background. Sign ups are added to your Shopify customers with email marketing consent. Typical use. A 10% welcome offer above the footer, over a lifestyle photo. Section background More settings More settings Content Panel Height Spam protection notice Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Content alignment | Custom height (desktop) | Custom height (mobile) | Email placeholder | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Height (desktop) | Height (mobile) | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Panel style | Panel top and bottom padding (desktop) | Panel top and bottom padding (mobile) | Panel width (desktop) | Panel width (mobile) | Section width | Submit label | Subtext | Success message | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Newsletter popup","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-newsletter-popup","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An email sign up popup that opens after a delay and comes back after the number of days you set once closed (0 shows it on every visit). The card is Tinted glass, Glass or Solid over a dimmed page. Sign ups are added to your Shopify customers with the tag newsletter . The home page template includes it; add it to other templates when you want it there too. Typical use. A welcome offer shown five seconds after arrival, once every 30 days. Content Spam protection notice","l":"Close button label (accessibility) | Color scheme | Email field placeholder | Enable popup | Heading | Legal text | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Open delay | Overlay opacity (desktop) | Overlay opacity (mobile) | Reappear after | Subheading | Submit button label (accessibility) | Success message"},{"t":"Social media links","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-socials","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A heading, the icons of your social media profiles and an optional button. The icons are the links typed once in Theme settings, Social media : only the networks with a URL show. The button, outlined or in glass, appears only when Button link is filled. Previous versions of Balm Studio named this section Socials. Typical use. An @yourbrand band with the Instagram, TikTok and Pinterest icons and a Follow us button, above the footer. Content Section background More settings More settings Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Color scheme | Gap between heading and button | Heading | Padding bottom | Padding top | Section width | Surface | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"FAQ","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement","u":"sections.html#s-faq","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A title column beside an accordion of FAQ item blocks (a question and a rich text answer), with an optional subheading and button. Alignment, gaps and row heights are set separately for desktop and mobile. The FAQ page template ( page.faq ) opens with it. Typical use. An FAQ page of eight to twelve questions on delivery, returns and ingredients, with a Contact us button under the title. Section background More settings More settings Alignment Spacing Questions","l":"Accordion content alignment (desktop) | Accordion content alignment (mobile) | Answer bottom padding (desktop) | Answer bottom padding (mobile) | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Color scheme | Gap between questions (desktop) | Gap between questions (mobile) | Gap between the two columns (desktop) | Gap between the two columns (mobile) | Header over this section | Heading | Heading column spacing (desktop) | Heading column spacing (mobile) | Heading level | Minimum height (desktop) | Minimum height (mobile) | Open several questions at once | Open the first question | Question row padding (desktop) | Question row padding (mobile) | Section heading alignment (desktop) | Section heading alignment (mobile) | Section width | Subheading | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: FAQ item","p":"Sections / Trust and engagement / FAQ","u":"sections.html#s-faq-item","x":"One question and its answer.","l":"Answer | Question"},{"t":"About page","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#about-page","x":"Four sections built for a brand story page. The About template ( page.about ) opens with them, and each one can be added to any other page too."},{"t":"Brand story hero","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-hero","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The opening section of the About page: a three part italic title, a heading, body text, a button and an image, on an inner panel over the section background. Typical use. The top of the About page, with the brand promise in the title and the founding story in two short paragraphs. Section background More settings Panel background Transparent header Spacing","l":"Allow transparent header | Body font size | Body text | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Color scheme | Dark overlay opacity | Heading | Heading level | Heading part 1 (light italic) | Heading part 2 (black italic) | Heading part 3 (italic) | Inner panel style | Left image (media) | Panel image | Panel image (mobile) | Section width | Surface | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Transparent header top padding (desktop) | Transparent header top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Comparison panels","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-problem-shift","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Two panels side by side, each with a title, a subtitle and body text, on an inner panel over the section background. Typical use. The problem on the left and how your product changes it on the right. Section background More settings More settings Inner panel Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Inner panel style | Left body | Left heading | Left subtitle | Right body | Right heading | Right subtitle | Section width | Surface | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Checklist banner","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-feels-off","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. An interactive checklist of Check item blocks that visitors tick, beside a heading, a subheading and a button. Once items are ticked, the button leads to the link of the first or last ticked item that has one, or to the button link. Typical use. A Does this sound like you? list of four situations, each linked to the product that answers it. Section background More settings Panel background Spacing","l":"Background image | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Checklist heading | Color scheme | Dark overlay opacity | Footer text | Heading | Inner panel style | Panel image | Panel image (mobile) | Section width | Subheading | Surface | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Check item","p":"Sections / About page / Checklist banner","u":"sections.html#s-about-feels-off-item","x":"One line of the checklist, with an optional link the button can take over.","l":"Item link (optional) | Item text"},{"t":"Gallery banner","p":"Sections / About page","u":"sections.html#s-about-community","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A background image crossed by a colored band with two large words, a link below the band, and a gallery of Element blocks (images, round or square, optionally linked) that scrolls sideways with arrows. Typical use. Photos from your community or your Instagram at the bottom of the About page. Background Colors Elements Spacing","l":"Background color | Background image | Background image (mobile) | Band color | Band text color | Band text size (desktop) | Band text size (mobile) | Banner word 1 | Banner word 2 | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Element size (desktop) | Element size (mobile) | Link URL (below the band) | Link color (desktop) | Link color (mobile) | Link label (below the band) | Overlay color | Overlay opacity | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Element","p":"Sections / About page / Gallery banner","u":"sections.html#s-about-community-element","x":"One image of the gallery, with an optional link and its own shape.","l":"Image | Link (optional)"},{"t":"Contact and stores","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#contact-and-stores","x":"Used by the Contact ( page.contact ) and Store locator ( page.find-us ) templates."},{"t":"Contact","p":"Sections / Contact and stores","u":"sections.html#s-contact","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. The Shopify contact form in a card, with a heading, a subtitle and a success message. Messages reach the email address of your store. The Contact page template ( page.contact ) uses it. Typical use. The Contact page, with a subtitle that gives your response time. Section background More settings More settings Heading and intro Spam protection notice Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Form width (desktop) | Header over this section | Heading | Heading level | Name and email fields (desktop) | Notice alignment | Notice color | Notice text size (desktop) | Notice text size (mobile) | Section width | Subtitle | Success message | Surface | Text color | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Store locator","p":"Sections / Contact and stores","u":"sections.html#s-find-us","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A store locator page over a background photo: two columns of Stores and Online lists (rich text, shown as accordions), and a map slot for an app block or a Custom Liquid block where you paste a store locator embed. The Store locator template ( page.find-us ) uses it. Typical use. A Where to buy page listing your retailers city by city, with the map of a store locator app. Background Spacing Store-locator map Accordion labels Column 1 Column 2","l":"\"Online\" label | \"Stores\" label | Background image | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Column 1 (online) | Column 1 (stores) | Column 1 heading | Column 2 (online) | Column 2 (stores) | Column 2 heading | Dark overlay opacity | Gap between columns (desktop) | Heading | Heading level | Map height (desktop) | Map height (mobile) | Section width | Show second column | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Block: Custom Liquid","p":"Sections / Contact and stores / Store locator","u":"sections.html#s-find-us-liquid","x":"Paste the embed code of a store locator service here. This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Liquid / HTML code"},{"t":"Layout, code and apps","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#layout-and-code","x":""},{"t":"Divider","p":"Sections / Layout, code and apps","u":"sections.html#s-divider","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. A line or an empty space between two sections, with its own height for desktop and mobile, line thickness, width and opacity. Typical use. A thin line between two sections that share the same background. Section background More settings More settings","l":"Background image (mobile) | Color scheme | Height (desktop) | Height (mobile) | Line opacity | Line thickness | Line width | Section width | Style | Surface"},{"t":"Custom Liquid","p":"Sections / Layout, code and apps","u":"sections.html#s-custom-liquid","x":"Where Any template. Not available in the header or footer group. Your own Liquid, HTML or app snippet in a section of its own, contained or full width, with the usual color scheme, background and spacing settings. Read Custom code before using it. Typical use. An embed code provided by a third party service that has no app block. Section background More settings More settings","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Header over this section | Liquid code | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Apps","p":"Sections / Layout, code and apps","u":"sections.html#s-apps","x":"Where Any template, and the header and footer groups. A container for app blocks, with a color scheme and spacing, and an option to remove the content width limit so an app can draw edge to edge. Typical use. Reviews carousel or Instagram feed from an app, placed between two sections of the home page. Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Section width | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Template sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#template-sections","x":"The main section of each template: what a product, collection, cart or blog page shows. Most of them cannot be removed from their template, but their settings are yours."},{"t":"Product","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-product","x":"Where Part of the product template. The product page: on one side a stage with the product name in layers around the cutout and Next formula , the name of the next product, which opens it; on the other a column of blocks (breadcrumb, title, rating, price, tagline, options, buy button, the product passport, collapsible rows, reviews and products that pair well). The whole page wears the product color, and choosing a variant that has its own colors recolors it. It is the main section of the product template, so it is not offered in Add section . Product: the stage and the column, in the color of the product. Product: the passport, six rows on two columns. Its settings and every block are documented on Product page blocks ."},{"t":"Product recommendations","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-product-recommendations","x":"Where Only on product templates. Product cards under the product page. Recommendation intent picks where they come from: Related (similar products) are generated by Shopify, Complementary (pairs well with) are the ones you curate in the Search & Discovery app, and Random from a collection shows products of the Collection you pick, in a new order on every visit. Fill up from the collection completes Shopify's recommendations from that collection when they are fewer than the maximum. Neither ever shows a product twice, nor the product of the page. The cards sit in a grid or a carousel per device, with the arrows of Theme settings, Carousels , and Badges picks which badges they show. Typical use. Four related products under every product page, with the custom badge showing on new formulas. Section background More settings Content Layout Cards Spacing","l":"Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Carousel navigation (desktop) | Carousel navigation (mobile) | Collection | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Fill up from the collection | Heading | Layout (desktop) | Layout (mobile) | Maximum products | Next card preview (mobile) | Recommendation intent | Section width | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Sticky add to cart","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-sticky-atc","x":"Where Only on product templates. A bar with the product thumbnail, title, selected variant, price and add to cart button that stays at the top or bottom of the screen, on desktop and mobile separately. By default it appears once the main buy button scrolls out of view. A variant that sells as a pre-order says Pre-order here too. The bar exists only as this section, which the product template places below the Product section. Preview versions of Balm Studio also offered it as a Sticky add to cart block inside the Product section; that block has been removed. Typical use. At the bottom of the screen on phones, where the main buy button quickly scrolls away. Displayed content Behavior","l":"Always visible | Enable the bar | Price (desktop) | Price (mobile) | Product thumbnail (desktop) | Product thumbnail (mobile) | Product title"},{"t":"Collection","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-collection","x":"Where Part of the collection template. The collection page: a banner with the title, description and image, an optional row of collection links, filters and sorting, and the product grid. Filters come from the Search & Discovery app and can sit in a column, a drawer or a horizontal bar, whose drawer style is set in Theme settings, Filters . Pagination is page numbers, a Load more button or infinite scroll. Visitors can change the column count when you allow it (see Column selector ), and Promo tile blocks take the place of a card on the first page. Badges picks the badges of the cards, and Text behind cutouts prints the product's title behind PNG and WebP pictures. It is the main section of the collection template, so it is not offered in Add section . The banner shows, in this order, the collection's custom.banner_image metafield, the Banner image set in the section, or the collection's own image. Shopify keeps no focal point on a collection's image: pick the picture in the section or in the metafield to frame it at the focal point set in Files. See Metafields, Banner image . Collection: tiles in the color of each product. Collection: the Index view, rows that preview each product","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Banner image | Banner position (desktop) | Banner position (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs alignment | Breadcrumbs on this page | Button label | Card content alignment | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card style | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Default view on desktop | Default view on mobile | Element order | Enable filters | Enable sorting | Feature the first product | Filter layout | Header over this section | Hover effect | Image banner height (desktop) | Image banner height (mobile) | Image fit | Image ratio | Let visitors change the column count (desktop) | Let visitors change the column count (mobile) | Let visitors switch between Grid and Index | Maximum swatches before \"+N\" | Menu | Overlay opacity (image banner) | Padding on the image (desktop) | Padding on the image (mobile) | Pagination | Position on the image (desktop) | Position on the image (mobile) | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Products per page | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Search box from | Second image on hover | Section width | Show collection image | Show collection title | Show color swatches | Show counts on filter values | Show description | Show draggable price range | Show results count | Show the product rating | Show vendor | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Surface | Swatch option name | Swatch shape | Swatch size | Text backdrop | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Values before \"Show more\""},{"t":"Block: Promo tile","p":"Sections / Template sections / Collection","u":"sections.html#s-main-collection-promo-tile","x":"A tile that takes the place of a product card at the position you choose, on the first page of the grid only. This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Button label | Color scheme | Heading | Image | Image (mobile) | Link | Position in the grid | Text | Text alignment | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Search","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-search","x":"Where Part of the search template. The search results page, with the same filters, sorting, pagination and product cards as the collection page. What it searches (products only, or products, articles and pages) is set in Theme settings, Search . Typical use. Filters in a drawer on every device, with infinite scroll. Section background More settings More settings Grid Filters and sorting Product cards Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Element order | Enable filters | Enable sorting | Field placeholder | Filter layout | Image fit | Image ratio | Pagination | Product title to price spacing (desktop) | Product title to price spacing (mobile) | Quick add | Quick add label | Quick view | Results layout | Results per page | Search box from | Second image on hover | Section width | Show color swatches | Show counts on filter values | Show draggable price range | Show results count | Show vendor | Spacing inside card (desktop) | Spacing inside card (mobile) | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Values before \"Show more\""},{"t":"Collections list","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-list-collections","x":"Where Part of the list of collections template. The page that lists your collections ( /collections ): every collection alphabetically, or only the ones you pick, in the order you pick them. Typical use. A curated list of six collections, with the product count on each card. Section background More settings More settings Heading Collections Layout Cards Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Collections per page | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Curated collections (optional) | Header over this section | Heading | Layout on desktop | Layout on mobile | Section width | Show heading | Show product count | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Cart","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-cart","x":"Where Part of the cart template. The cart page: the lines beside a summary that follows the scroll, with quantity rules, the order note, the discount code, the free shipping bar, the totals and the accelerated checkout buttons. It works without JavaScript. What it shows is set once for the page and the drawer in Theme settings, Cart ; the section keeps its color scheme, width and background. Gift wrapping appears here when it is on in Theme settings. Typical use. An order note for delivery instructions and the accelerated checkout buttons under the checkout button. Section background More settings More settings This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Color scheme | Section width | Surface"},{"t":"Cart drawer","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-cart-drawer","x":"Where Part of every page. It is listed in the theme editor and cannot be removed or moved. The panel that slides in when a product is added to the cart, or the short notification that replaces it. It has no settings of its own: its type, style, free shipping bar, recommendations, order note, discount code and checkout buttons are set in Theme settings, Cart , shared with the cart page. The free shipping bar only displays progress toward the amount you type. It does not create free shipping or a discount: set the real rule in your admin (Settings, Shipping and delivery, or Discounts) and keep the two amounts the same. Cart drawer: a sheet in the color of the last product added. Typical use. A floating glass drawer with a free shipping bar at 50 in your currency, three complementary suggestions in a carousel and the order note."},{"t":"Blog","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-blog","x":"Where Part of the blog template. The blog page: article cards with image, date, author, excerpt and tags, an optional row of tag filters, and page numbers. Typical use. Three columns on desktop, one on mobile, with the tag filter row for recipes and news. Section background More settings More settings Layout Cards Metadata Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Articles per page | Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Excerpt length (words) | Header over this section | Section width | Show author | Show date | Show excerpt | Show featured image | Show tag filter row | Show tags on cards | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Article","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-article","x":"Where Part of the article template. A blog post: featured image, date, author, tags, share buttons, links to the previous and next posts, and comments when the blog allows them, in a reading column whose width and type sizes you set. Typical use. A reading column of about 700 px with the share buttons and the previous and next links. Section background More settings More settings Content Comments Reading column Typography Spacing Breadcrumbs This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Body text size (desktop) | Body text size (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs alignment | Breadcrumbs on this page | Color scheme | Column width (desktop) | Column width (mobile) | Comments per page | Header over this section | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Section width | Show author | Show date | Show featured image | Show previous / next articles | Show share buttons | Show tags | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Page","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-page","x":"Where Part of the page template. A standard page from your admin (Online Store, Pages) in a reading column, with its title and content. Typical use. Legal pages, shipping information and other text pages. Section background More settings More settings Reading column Typography Spacing This section accepts app blocks.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Body text size (desktop) | Body text size (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Color scheme | Column width (desktop) | Column width (mobile) | Content width | Header over this section | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Page title alignment (desktop) | Page title alignment (mobile) | Section width | Show page title | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"404 page","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-404","x":"Where Part of the 404 template. The page shown when a link is broken: a heading, a message, a button home, an optional search bar and a few products from a collection of your choice. Typical use. A friendly message, the search bar and four best sellers to keep the visitor in the store. Section background More settings More settings Content Search Featured collection Typography Spacing","l":"Background image (mobile) | Badges | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Collection | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Featured heading | Header over this section | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Home button label | Message | Products shown | Search button label | Search placeholder | Section width | Show search bar | Surface | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Password page","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-password","x":"Where Part of the password template. The page visitors see while your store is password protected, with your logo, the password form and a background. The message above the form is set in Online Store, Preferences. Typical use. A coming soon page before launch. Branding Content Background Typography Spacing","l":"Background image | Extra bottom padding (desktop) | Extra bottom padding (mobile) | Extra top padding (desktop) | Extra top padding (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Image overlay opacity | Logo image | Logo width (desktop) | Logo width (mobile) | Password field label | Password placeholder | Section width | Submit button label"},{"t":"Gift card","p":"Sections / Template sections","u":"sections.html#s-main-gift-card","x":"Where Part of the gift card template. The page a customer opens from their gift card email, with the card value, the code, a QR code, and buttons to copy the code, print the page and go to the store. Typical use. Your logo on top, on your main color scheme. Section background More settings More settings Branding Content Typography Spacing Three more sections exist in the theme files without appearing in the section list: Quick view, Predictive search and Pickup availability. They have no settings; the theme loads them on demand to fill the quick view modal, the search suggestions and the pickup details. Quick view is configured in Theme settings, Quick view , predictive search in the Header section. Preview versions of Balm Studio also offered a Lifestyle strip section, two photos side by side in one rounded card. It has been removed.","l":"Background image (mobile) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Code hint | Color scheme | Copy button label | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Logo image | Print button label | QR code hint | Section width | Shop button label | Surface | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Blocks used inside sections","p":"Sections","u":"sections.html#blocks","x":"Blocks that several sections accept, and the blocks that build the header mega menus."},{"t":"Theme blocks","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections","u":"sections.html#theme-blocks","x":"General purpose blocks accepted by Image with text, Rich text and the product information column. Stack them in any order to build a content column."},{"t":"Heading","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-heading","x":"A heading. Heading level (semantic) sets the level for search engines and screen readers without changing the size.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Heading level (semantic) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text | Typography style"},{"t":"Text","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-text","x":"A rich text paragraph, with an optional maximum width.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Limit text width | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Max text width | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Text"},{"t":"Button","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-button","x":"A link styled as a Solid, Outline or Glass button, or as a text link.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Label | Link | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Open in a new tab | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Style"},{"t":"Image","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-image","x":"An image with a ratio, a width, an optional height limit and a corner radius.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Corner radius | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Image | Limit height | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Max height (desktop) | Max height (mobile) | Ratio | Width (desktop) | Width (mobile)"},{"t":"Spacer","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-spacer","x":"Empty space, with its own height on desktop and mobile.","l":"Height (desktop) | Height (mobile)"},{"t":"Liquid","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Theme blocks","u":"sections.html#tb-liquid","x":"Your own Liquid or HTML. See Custom code .","l":"Liquid code"},{"t":"Mega menu blocks","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections","u":"sections.html#mega-menu-blocks","x":"A mega menu is a panel that opens under a top level item of the main menu. Add a Mega menu block to the Header section, type the exact title of that menu item in Linked menu item , then add the blocks below inside it. On phones the panel becomes an accordion in the mobile menu."},{"t":"Mega menu","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-menu","x":"The panel itself: which menu item opens it, its layout, width, background and padding. Layout builds the panel from the sub-links of the linked menu item ( Links and images , Images only or Links only ) or from the blocks you add inside it ( Custom blocks ). With Custom blocks, the blocks sit on one row of the panel and wrap onto a new row when they do not fit, exactly Block spacing (desktop) apart. Each block has a Width (desktop) : Auto (its content), 1/4, 1/3, 1/2, 2/3 or Fill (what the others leave). Horizontal alignment (desktop) and Vertical alignment (desktop) place them when they leave room. Media height (desktop) on Match tallest, the default, gives every block with a picture the height of the tallest one, text under the picture included, so every bottom lines up; Fixed uses the height you set. In the mobile menu the links come first, then the cards (Promo, Image and each card of Image cards), all of the same width and Card ratio (mobile) , laid out by Mobile cards layout : Carousel (one row that scrolls sideways, the next card showing), Grid (two columns) or Stack. Grid Mobile menu Panel dimensions Inner padding Accepts these blocks inside it: Link column, Image, Image ca","l":"Block spacing (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Card ratio (mobile) | Card spacing (mobile) | Carousel card width (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Height (desktop) | Horizontal alignment (desktop) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Layout | Link columns | Linked menu item | Links width (desktop) | Max width (desktop) | Media height (desktop) | Mobile cards layout | Panel background | Panel width (desktop) | Products per category | Show product count | Show product lists on mobile | Show product preview | Top padding (desktop) | Vertical alignment (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Link column","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-column","x":"A list of links. Menu picks one of your menus, the header's main menu when empty. Links shows All links, or Only the links under a Parent link , by default the item the mega menu opens from. Heading defaults to the title of the parent link; in the mobile menu the heading folds the links like an accordion, and without it they show at once. Second and third level links get a Sub-link indent . Group spacing sets the space between the first level links, each with the links under it, and Link spacing the space between the links under them, on desktop and on mobile. Show thumbnails puts the picture of each product and collection link before it, with its size and corner radius; the other links keep its room, so the texts line up. Layout Spacing Typography Thumbnails","l":"Group spacing (desktop) | Group spacing (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading to links spacing (desktop) | Heading to links spacing (mobile) | Link size (desktop) | Link size (mobile) | Link spacing (desktop) | Link spacing (mobile) | Links | Menu | Parent link | Show heading (desktop) | Show heading (mobile) | Show thumbnails (desktop) | Show thumbnails (mobile) | Sub-link indent (desktop) | Sub-link indent (mobile) | Sub-link size (desktop) | Sub-link size (mobile) | Thumbnail corner radius | Thumbnail size (desktop) | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Thumbnails for | Vertical padding (desktop) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Image","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-image","x":"An image with an optional caption, subtitle and link label, under the picture or on it, cropped at its focal point. Nothing shows on the storefront without a picture. Layout Image crop Spacing Caption Typography Mobile","l":"Caption | Caption alignment | Caption size (desktop) | Caption size (mobile) | Caption top spacing (desktop) | Crop | Image | Image / caption gap (mobile) | Image alignment (desktop) | Image height (desktop) | Image ratio (desktop) | Image width (desktop) | Link | Link label | Show in the mobile menu | Subtitle | Subtitle size (desktop) | Subtitle size (mobile) | Vertical padding (desktop) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Image cards","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-cards","x":"A row of up to four picture cards. Image source set to Automatic shows the picture of what each sub-link of the linked menu item points to: a collection or a product (with its price), a blog post, or a page through its custom.image metafield (see Metafields, Page image ). Custom cards shows the Image card blocks you add inside it. Every picture is cropped at its focal point, in the Image ratio (desktop) you pick (Original, Square, three portrait and three landscape ratios, or a fixed height), with the media corner radius of Theme settings or your own, and a Hover effect (Zoom, Fade or None). The text sits below the picture or on it: on the picture, place it in one of nine positions per device and add a Text backdrop (Soft gradient or Soft glow) only where the text is, so it reads on any photo. Images Text Typography Mobile menu Accepts these blocks inside it: Image card.","l":"Button style | Card width (desktop) | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Hover effect | Image height (desktop) | Image ratio (desktop) | Image source | Number of cards | Show cards in the mobile menu | Space between image and heading | Spacing (desktop) | Subtitle size (desktop) | Subtitle size (mobile) | Text alignment | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Image card","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-card","x":"One card of an Image cards block set to Custom cards: an image, a heading, a subtitle, a link and an optional button label.","l":"Button label | Heading | Image | Link | Subtitle"},{"t":"Products","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-products","x":"Two to four products as mini cards with image, title and price. With Show product tagline on in the Header section, each card also shows the product's custom.tagline metafield. Grid Thumbnails Content Mobile","l":"Card alignment | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Grid columns (desktop) | Grid columns (mobile) | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading top spacing (desktop) | Heading top spacing (mobile) | Price size (desktop) | Price size (mobile) | Products | Show (mobile) | Show price | Thumbnail crop | Thumbnail ratio | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Promo","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-promo","x":"An image tile with a heading, a short text and a link. Image Layout Typography Spacing Mobile","l":"Alignment | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading top spacing (desktop) | Heading top spacing (mobile) | Image | Image fit | Image ratio | Link | Link label | Show (mobile) | Text | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text top spacing (desktop) | Text top spacing (mobile) | Tile max width (desktop) | Vertical padding (desktop) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Banner","p":"Sections / Blocks used inside sections / Mega menu blocks","u":"sections.html#mm-mega-banner","x":"A wide banner with a background image, a heading, a short text and a button or link. Dimensions Background image Content Typography Button Mobile","l":"Background crop | Button label | Button size (desktop) | Button size (mobile) | Button style | Button top spacing (desktop) | Button top spacing (mobile) | Content horizontal alignment | Content vertical alignment | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Horizontal padding (desktop) | Horizontal padding (mobile) | Image | Link | Max text width (desktop) | Max text width (mobile) | Minimum height (desktop) | Minimum height (mobile) | Ratio (optional) | Short text | Show (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Text top spacing (desktop) | Text top spacing (mobile) | Vertical padding (desktop) | Vertical padding (mobile) | Width (desktop)"},{"t":"Product page blocks","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html","x":"Balm Studio ships one product page, and every product uses it. You shape it from the theme editor, and you can let each product carry its own colors and texts through metafields, so you never need a second template."},{"t":"How the page is built","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#how-it-is-built","x":"The Product section is a two column layout: the media gallery on one side, a column of blocks on the other. Add, remove and reorder the blocks in the theme editor: Online Store, Themes, Customize , then pick Products in the page menu at the top. The section also accepts app blocks , so any app that offers a block (reviews, subscriptions, bundles) drops straight into the column, and the general theme blocks (Heading, Button, Spacer and the others). The template, templates/product.json , starts with this stack: Blocks marked shown only when render nothing on products that do not need them, so the page stays short even though the stack is long. The template carries no example text: a block whose text is empty shows nothing on the storefront, not even its spacing, and a dimmed example in the theme editor. Below the section, the template places, as on the demo store, a Slideshow , the Sticky add to cart bar, Key ingredients , a Routine , Before and after , Compare products , an FAQ , Testimonials and Product recommendations . Fill them, or remove the ones you do not need. Add an Icon list block for reassurance claims under the buy buttons. The Product section is the main section of the "},{"t":"Buy button styles","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#buy-button-styles","x":"The Style setting of the Buy buttons block offers five looks. Each keeps its own Corner radius , Font weight and Letter case settings, so you can land anywhere between them. Welding joins the buy button to the Packs menu variant picker so the two read as one shape. It needs the Signature pill style, because the seam depends on its square corner. Turn on Weld to the buy button in the Variant picker block and Weld to the packs menu in the Buy buttons block."},{"t":"About the Glass style","p":"Product page blocks / Buy button styles","u":"product-page.html#glass-style","x":"Glass takes its recipe from Theme settings, Glass effect : one tint, one opacity, one blur and one border opacity, shared by every glass surface. Change it once and the buy button, the upsell buttons, the popup trigger, the newsletter card and the cart panel move together. The label keeps the text color of the section's color scheme. Balm Studio measures the contrast between that color and the frosted surface, and only when it falls below 3:1 (the WCAG floor for large text) does it switch the label to black or white, whichever reads better. Over a background image or a gradient the backdrop changes from pixel to pixel, so the theme leaves your scheme color alone there: check the contrast yourself. Glass is available on the buy button, on the Product upsell buttons ( Button style , separate from the card style) and on the Popup trigger."},{"t":"Variant picker styles","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#variant-picker-styles","x":"Swatch styles fall back to a text pill for option values with no swatch saved. Unavailable option values grays out or hides combinations that cannot be bought. Products that belong to a combined listing switch to the sibling product when a shopper picks one of its values: see Combined listings ."},{"t":"Ready-made backgrounds","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#backgrounds","x":"The Product section can paint its own background. The setting is Background mode , at the top of the section settings, with six modes: None (use the color scheme) , Solid color , Gradient (two colors) , Image , Radial halo and Product gradient (metafields) . The template default is None (use the color scheme) . The three combinations below are ready to copy, and the fourth, Product gradient , gives every product its own colors with nothing to connect."},{"t":"A. Soft gradient","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-soft-gradient","x":"A near white wash that lifts the packshot without coloring it. These gradient colors are already typed into the template, so switching the mode is all it takes."},{"t":"B. Warm paper","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-warm-paper","x":"A single flat color. The calmest option, and the easiest to connect to a metafield so each product carries its own shade."},{"t":"C. Radial halo","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-radial-halo","x":"A dark halo anchored in one corner over a light base. The most dramatic of the three; use it when the packshot is cut out on a transparent background. To give every product its own background color, connect these colors to product metafields: the step by step guide is on Metafields . For a gradient, the Product gradient mode below does it without any connection."},{"t":"D. Product gradient","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-product-gradient","x":"Each product paints its own gradient from two Color metafields, read directly: custom.background_color for the start and custom.background_color_end for the end. There is nothing to connect in the theme editor: create the two definitions once (see Metafields ), fill them on each product, and choose the mode. Both colors filled : the gradient runs from the first to the second, in the direction set. One color filled : the section is that one color. Neither : the background of the section's color scheme, as in None. Fallback background color plays no part in this mode. The Sticky add to cart bar takes the end color as its accent, as in the Gradient mode. The Products showcase spotlights read the same two metafields, and Featured set the first one, so a product keeps its colors from the home page to its own page."},{"t":"Extend the gradient under the header","p":"Product page blocks / Ready-made backgrounds","u":"product-page.html#bg-under-header","x":"Over a hero, a transparent header lets the image run to the top of the screen. The product page can do the same with its gradient. The setting is Extend the background under the header , shown in the Product gradient mode, off by default. It needs two conditions: the Header section has Header behavior on Transparent at top or Adaptive ; the Product section is the first section of the product template, as it is in the templates Balm Studio ships. The gradient then starts at the top of the screen, under the header and under a Floating or Glass announcement bar. A Solid announcement bar in full width keeps its place above it. The header is transparent at rest and takes its card on scroll, as it does over a hero. The product content and the breadcrumbs stay clear of it: the section adds the height of the header to its top padding. Without either condition, the setting has no effect. Whatever its Section width , the Product section keeps its background edge to edge; Section width moves the product content only. There is nothing to choose for the header's colors: it reads each product's gradient where it lies under the header. Over a dark gradient it takes its Colors over dark background"},{"t":"Sticky columns","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#sticky-columns","x":"Sticky columns (desktop) , in the Layout group of the Product section, is on by default. From 768 px wide, the shorter of the two columns, the gallery or the product information, stays in view under the header while the other one scrolls, and the end of the section releases it. A column taller than the screen scrolls until its bottom shows, then holds. On phones the columns stack and nothing is sticky. The setting was named Sticky product info in preview versions, when only the information column could hold."},{"t":"Text behind cutout images","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#text-behind-cutouts","x":"The Product section can print a large decorative text behind the cutout images of its gallery: PNG and WebP images, whose transparent areas let the text show through. JPG images, videos and 3D models stay as they are. The theme knows a cutout by its file format only, so a PNG without transparency also gets the text, hidden behind its opaque pixels. The settings are in the Text behind cutouts group, off by default. Check Show on desktop , Show on mobile , or both. Desktop starts at 768 px wide. Choose the Text : Product title (the default), Product tagline (custom.tagline) , read from the product's metafield, or Custom text , the same on every product. A product whose tagline is empty shows no text. Set Apply to : First image only (the default) shows the text when the first media of the gallery is a PNG or WebP image; All cutout images puts it behind every one. Style it: Font (heading or body font), Font weight (Bold by default), Text case (UPPERCASE by default), Text size (160 px on desktop, 80 px on mobile) and the Vertical position and Horizontal position of each device (centered by default). Pick the Text color : Color scheme text , Gradient end color (custom.background_color_en"},{"t":"The accelerated checkout buttons","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#accelerated-checkout","x":"With Dynamic checkout buttons on, the wallet buttons (Shop Pay, PayPal, Google Pay, Apple Pay) show under Add to cart. Which ones appear depends on the payment methods your store has enabled and on the visitor's browser, so the row differs from one shopper to the next. The row follows the selected variant: it is hidden while that variant is sold out or unavailable and comes back as soon as a variant that can be bought is chosen. A pre-order variant can be bought, so it keeps the row. Quick view and the sticky add to cart bar have no accelerated checkout buttons. These buttons are drawn by Shopify, inside an element no theme and no app can style directly. Shopify exposes a short list of settings instead, and Balm Studio sets all of them from your Add to cart button: No theme can change the brand color of each button, its logo, its label or its font: Shop Pay stays purple and PayPal yellow on every Shopify store. Because Shopify caps the wallet height at 55 px, a Button height above 55 makes Add to cart taller than the wallet row; keep it at 55 or below if you want the two to match. The cart drawer and the cart page get the same treatment."},{"t":"Product section settings","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#product-section-settings","x":"Settings of the Product section itself: background (with the product metafields they connect to, and the Product gradient that reads them directly), product vignette, bottom curve, layout ( sticky columns and one collapsible row open at a time), gallery, badges on media, packshot captions, text behind cutouts , video and 3D, spacing and breadcrumbs. The spacing between collapsible rows is set on each row. Select the section in the editor, above its blocks, to see them. Section background Image settings Background illustration Scene Layout Media Gallery layout Packshot captions Video and 3D Spacing Breadcrumbs","l":"Autoplay videos | Background illustration | Background image | Badges on media | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Breadcrumbs alignment | Breadcrumbs on this page | Caption alignment | Caption case | Caption color | Caption size (desktop) | Caption size (mobile) | Caption source | Caption weight | Carousel position indicator | Color scheme | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Desktop layout | Extend the background under the header | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Gallery arrows | Gap between media (desktop) | Gap between media (mobile) | Illustration horizontal alignment (desktop) | Illustration horizontal alignment (mobile) | Illustration horizontal offset (desktop) | Illustration horizontal offset (mobile) | Illustration opacity | Illustration vertical alignment (desktop) | Illustration vertical alignment (mobile) | Illustration vertical offset (desktop) | Illustration vertical offset (mobile) | Illustration width (desktop) | Illustration width (mobile) | Loop videos | Maximum zoom level | Media controls style | Media corner radius | Media ratio (desktop) | Media ratio (mobile) | Metafield | Mobile layout | Mute videos | Next-slide peek (mobile) | One collapsible row open at a time | Scene height (mobile) | Scene width (desktop) | Section width | Show background illustration | Show captions | Show the AR button on 3D models | Show thumbnails | Show video controls | Space above the caption | Sticky scene (desktop) | Style | Surface | Thumbnail size | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Viewer height (desktop) | Zoom image"},{"t":"Blocks","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#blocks","x":"Every block of the product information column, with the name the block picker shows. Settings that can be connected to a product metafield say so in their notes, with the exact definition to create; the full list is on Metafields . Breadcrumb Product title Vendor Price SKU Rating Reviews Text Variant picker Volume pricing Purchase options Gift card recipient Buy buttons Stock status Back in stock Pickup availability Payment icons Product upsell Complementary products Description Collapsible row Popup Specifications Specification Icon list Icon item Image Badge Share Next product Liquid"},{"t":"Breadcrumb","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-crumb","x":"A short breadcrumb above the title, for example Shop / Night cream : your Label with its Link , then the product type. It replaces the full breadcrumb trail on the product page of the demo.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Label | Link | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Product title","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-title","x":"The product title, the main heading of the page. Keep one Title block on H1; any extra title block should use a subheading level.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading level | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Typography style"},{"t":"Vendor","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-vendor","x":"The brand or maker name, from the product admin page.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Price","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-price","x":"The price, the compare-at price, the unit price and an optional taxes and shipping note. It follows the selected variant.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show compare-at price | Show unit price | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Taxes and shipping note | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"SKU","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-sku","x":"The SKU of the selected variant, with an optional prefix.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Prefix | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Rating","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-rating","x":"Stars, the numeric value and the review count, read from the standard reviews.rating and reviews.rating_count metafields that review apps fill. It renders nothing until an app fills them. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show the numeric value | Show the review count | Star color | Star size (desktop) | Star size (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Reviews","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-reviews","x":"Two short reviews under the product details, each a quote and the name of the customer. Type only real reviews; a review without its quote is not shown on your store. For reviews collected by an app, use its app block instead. Typography Spacing","l":"First review | First reviewer's name | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Second review | Second reviewer's name | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile)"},{"t":"Text","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-text","x":"A free rich text paragraph, the same on every product, or with Source set to Tagline , the product's own custom.tagline metafield, read directly. Empty, it shows nothing on the storefront.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Source | Text | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Variant picker","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-variant-picker","x":"The options the customer chooses from, in one of six styles (see Variant picker styles ). It handles products with many variants, combined listings and unavailable combinations. Swatches Unavailable combinations Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Recolor the store with the variant | Show a price per option | Show option names | Show the selected value next to the option name | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Unavailable option values | Weld to the buy button"},{"t":"Volume pricing","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-volume-pricing","x":"Quantity price breaks, as a table or a list. It renders nothing when the variant has none. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show heading | Show the price for the chosen quantity | Style | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Purchase options","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-selling-plans","x":"One-time purchase and subscription options from your subscription app, with the plan names, descriptions and savings. It renders nothing unless the product has a selling plan. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | One-time purchase label | Show the plan description | Show the plan group name | Show the savings | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Gift card recipient","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-gift-card-recipient","x":"Lets the buyer send a gift card to someone else, with a name, an email, a message and a send date. It only renders on gift card products. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Toggle label | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Buy buttons","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-buy-buttons","x":"The quantity selector, Add to cart, the accelerated checkout buttons and the Shop Pay Installments banner. The quantity selector is the only one of the product page: Quantity selector (desktop) and Quantity selector (mobile) place it Above the buttons (the default), Inline with Add to cart, or Hidden, with its style, size and label; it follows the quantity rules of each variant and volume pricing. Preview versions of Balm Studio had a separate Quantity block; it has been removed. The accelerated checkout buttons (Buy it now and the wallets) are hidden while the selected variant is sold out and come back with a variant in stock; a pre-order variant can be bought, so it keeps them, and its button reads Pre-order. See Buy button styles , accelerated checkout and Pre-order . Quantity selector","l":"Add to cart label | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button height | Button size | Dynamic checkout buttons | Font weight | Full width Add to cart | Letter case | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Quantity selector (desktop) | Quantity selector (mobile) | Quantity selector size | Quantity selector style | Shop Pay Installments banner | Show quantity label | Sold out label | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Unavailable label | Weld to the packs menu"},{"t":"Stock status","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-inventory","x":"In stock, low stock or out of stock for the selected variant, with a colored dot and an optional exact quantity. Low stock only applies when inventory is tracked and the variant stops selling at zero. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | In-stock label | Low stock threshold | Low-stock label | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Out-of-stock label | Show the exact quantity | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Back in stock","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-notify-me","x":"A back in stock form, shown only while the selected variant is sold out. Requests arrive as contact form messages, at the store address set in Settings, Notifications, and name the exact variant; no app is needed. Style Spacing","l":"Ask for a name | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Email placeholder | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show heading | Subtext | Success message | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Pickup availability","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-pickup","x":"Local pickup availability for the selected variant, and a button that opens the list of locations. It renders nothing unless a location has pickup enabled. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Payment icons","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-payment-icons","x":"A reassurance line and the icons of the payment methods enabled in your store (Settings, Payments). A theme cannot add or reorder these icons; to show another badge, upload it as the block image. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Icon size | Image | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show the reassurance line | Space between icons | Text | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Product upsell","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-upsell","x":"Frequently bought together: products to buy alongside this one, from Shopify recommendations or your own selection. Bundle (tick boxes, one total) adds every ticked product in one action; Simple list (add one by one) gives each product its own button. The block takes the look of the product cards. Card style is Card (filled with the secondary background of the color scheme), Bordered (a fine outline, the default) or Plain (no box), with the corner radius of the cards set in Theme settings, Corner style . Thumbnails are square and never cropped, with their own size on desktop (72 px) and on mobile (64 px). In the bundle list, each row shows a checkbox, the thumbnail, the title and the price, with a quiet variant menu underneath for products with options, and a thin rule between rows; a Total line and a full width button close the block. Button style is Solid or Glass, separate from the card style. Source Layout Content Style Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Bundle button label | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Heading | Layout | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Number of products | Presentation | Products | Products come from | Products with several variants | Recommendation intent | Row button label | Show compare-at price | Show heading | Show price | Show product image | Space between products (desktop) | Space between products (mobile) | Thumbnail size (desktop) | Thumbnail size (mobile) | Tick every product by default | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Complementary products","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-complementary","x":"A small grid of product cards: complementary products from Shopify recommendations, curated in the Search & Discovery app, or your own selection, which can be connected to a product list metafield. Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Card gap (desktop) | Card gap (mobile) | Card title size (desktop) | Card title size (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Heading | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Number of products | Products | Products come from | Show heading | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Description","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-description","x":"The product description from the product admin page.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Collapsible row","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-collapsible-row","x":"An accordion row whose content is rich text, which can be connected to a metafield, or a page, to share one policy page across every product. A row without heading or content shows nothing on the storefront. Style is Lines (the default: heading on the left, icon on the right, thin rules and no frame), Boxed (a framed row) or Filled (the secondary background of the color scheme). Open and close icon is a Chevron that turns over, or a Plus that becomes a minus. The heading has its alignment, its size on desktop and on mobile, and its weight; Inner padding and Space between rows (desktop) and (mobile) are set per device too. Space between rows only shows with Boxed and Filled: stacked Lines rows share one rule between them. Set the style on each row, and give the rows of one stack the same values. Open by default opens the row when the page loads: check it on the first row to show its content at once. To let only one row stay open, turn on One collapsible row open at a time in the Product section. Rows open with a short animation where the browser supports it, and at once for visitors who ask for reduced motion. Style Spacing","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Content | Content comes from | Heading | Heading alignment | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading weight | Icon | Icon size | Inner padding (desktop) | Inner padding (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Open and close icon | Open by default | Page | Space between rows (desktop) | Space between rows (mobile) | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Popup","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-popup","x":"A link or button that opens a dialog with rich text or a page. The Under-title link style sits right below the product title. Without content, it shows nothing on the storefront. Modal content Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Content | Content comes from | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Margin top (desktop) | Margin top (mobile) | Modal heading | Modal width | Page | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Trigger label | Trigger style"},{"t":"Specifications","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-specs","x":"A label and value table built from Specification blocks, with lines, dots or zebra stripes between rows. Style Typography Spacing Accepts these blocks inside it: Specification.","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Gap between columns (desktop) | Gap between columns (mobile) | Heading | Label size (desktop) | Label size (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Row padding (desktop) | Row padding (mobile) | Row separator | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile) | Value alignment | Value size (desktop) | Value size (mobile)"},{"t":"Specification","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-spec-row","x":"One row of the Specifications block. Both the label and the value can be connected to product metafields.","l":"Label | Value"},{"t":"Icon list","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-icon-list","x":"Reassurance claims built from Icon item blocks, stacked, side by side, or on one row with a button. Icon stroke (Light, Regular, Medium or Bold) sets the line weight of the built in icons; your own images keep theirs. Heading weight and Body text weight set the weight of the two lines of text, and Alignment (desktop) and Alignment (mobile) place each claim, icon and text together, on the left, in the center or on the right of its column. Icon sizes, text sizes and gaps have a desktop and a mobile value. Icon and text gap (desktop) and (mobile) set the space the eye sees between each icon and its text, from the bottom of the icon to the top of the capitals: at 0 the letters touch the icon. Layout Typography Spacing Accepts these blocks inside it: Icon item.","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Alignment (mobile) | Body text size (desktop) | Body text size (mobile) | Body text weight | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Button label | Button link | Button style | Button text size (desktop) | Button text size (mobile) | Columns (desktop) | Columns (mobile) | Gap between items (desktop) | Gap between items (mobile) | Heading | Heading size (desktop) | Heading size (mobile) | Heading weight | Icon and text gap (desktop) | Icon and text gap (mobile) | Icon size (desktop) | Icon size (mobile) | Icon stroke | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Space before the button | Style | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Icon item","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-icon-item","x":"One claim of the Icon list: a built in glyph or your own image, a Heading and a Text . Heading and Text are rich text fields: press Enter for a new line, or connect a product metafield of type Single line text or Multi-line text with the dynamic source icon, each line of a Multi-line text on its own line. The Icon image connects to a File metafield the same way, so each product shows its own claims. See Icon metafields . An item with neither heading nor text stays hidden on the storefront.","l":"Earlier heading | Earlier text | Glyph | Heading | Icon image | Icon type | Text"},{"t":"Image","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-image","x":"An image inside the information column, with an optional caption. Connect it to a metafield to show a different image per product. Caption Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Aspect ratio | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Caption | Fit (when a ratio is set) | Image | Image width (desktop) | Image width (mobile) | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Space above the caption | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Badge","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-badge","x":"Automatic (Sale, Sold out, New, Custom) , the default, shows the same badges as the product cards, styled in Theme settings, Product badges, and nothing when none applies. Sale and Sold out follow the selected variant, and the Custom badge wears the product's own colors when its custom.badge_color or custom.badge_text_color metafield is filled (see badge colors ). Image places your own artwork in a corner of the product area. Spacing","l":"Badge type | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Edge offset (desktop) | Edge offset (mobile) | Image | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Position | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Share","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-share","x":"Share links for X, Facebook and Pinterest, and a copy link button. Spacing","l":"Alignment (desktop) | Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Label | Margin bottom (desktop) | Margin bottom (mobile) | Show Facebook | Show Pinterest | Show X | Show copy link | Show label | Text size (desktop) | Text size (mobile) | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"Next product","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-nav","x":"Links to the previous and next product of a collection (the product's first collection by default). Only the first 50 products of the collection are read. Layout","l":"Collection | Loop around | Next label | Show product names | Show the next product | Size (desktop) | Size (mobile)"},{"t":"Liquid","p":"Product page blocks / Blocks","u":"product-page.html#pb-product-liquid","x":"Your own Liquid or HTML, or the insertion code of an app that has no app block. See Custom code .","l":"Bottom padding (desktop) | Bottom padding (mobile) | Liquid code | Top padding (desktop) | Top padding (mobile)"},{"t":"When one product needs a different layout","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#second-template","x":"Metafields let one template carry different colors, texts and images per product. Some settings cannot be connected to a metafield: sliders, checkboxes, dropdowns, the color scheme and Liquid code. When a product needs a different value for one of those, create a second template: in the theme editor, open Products in the page menu, choose Create template , base it on the default product template, then assign it to the product from its admin page, under Theme template ."},{"t":"Products that used an older template","p":"Product page blocks","u":"product-page.html#older-templates","x":"Early versions of Balm Studio shipped extra product templates. They have been folded into the default one. A product still assigned to one of them falls back to the default product template and renders normally. To clear the setting, open the product in the admin and choose Default product under Theme template ."},{"t":"Features","p":"Features","u":"features.html","x":"The features that span several sections or the whole store: what they do, where to turn them on and what to know before you rely on them."},{"t":"Quick view","p":"Features","u":"features.html#quick-view","x":"Quick view opens a product in a modal from its card, so shoppers choose a variant and add to cart without leaving the page. The modal shows the gallery with thumbnails, the price with its badges and unit price, the rating, the same variant picker as the product page (swatches included), quantity rules, purchase options, the add to cart button, pickup availability, a short description and a link to the full product page. Adding to cart opens the cart drawer."},{"t":"Turn it on","p":"Features / Quick view","u":"features.html#quick-view-on","x":"Open a section that shows product cards: Collection, Featured collection, Search, Recently viewed or Lookbook. Set Quick view to Show on hover or Always show . On touch screens the button is always visible. In Theme settings, Quick view , choose what the modal shows and its card style: Solid, Tinted glass or Glass. Short description metafield takes the namespace and key of a product metafield, for example custom.short_description ; products without it show the first paragraph of their description, cut to Description length . Preload on hover loads the product when the pointer rests on its card so the modal opens at once, at the cost of more data. Without JavaScript the button simply opens the product page. Quick view is separate from Quick add , the setting that puts an add to cart button on the card itself: Off, Single-variant products, or All products (which opens an option picker for products with variants)."},{"t":"Product badges","p":"Features","u":"features.html#product-badges","x":"Four badges can appear on product cards, in quick view, in Compare products and on the product page. Every one of them states a fact of the product: nothing shows a text typed once for all products. Their position, shape and colors are set once in Theme settings, Product badges .","l":"Custom | New | Sale | Sold out"},{"t":"Set up the Custom badge","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#custom-badge","x":"Create the custom.badge_label definition once, as described in Metafields, Badge label . Fill it on the products that need a badge, for example Limited edition or Vegan . Leave it empty on the others. That is all: the cards, quick view, Compare products and the product page read the metafield directly. There is no key to type and nothing to connect in the theme editor."},{"t":"Give one product its own badge colors","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#custom-badge-colors","x":"The Custom badge wears the Custom background and Custom text colors of Theme settings. To color it differently on one product, for example green on a vegan product, create two optional product metafields of type Color : custom.badge_color for the background and custom.badge_text_color for the text (see Metafields, Badge colors ). They change the Custom badge of that product only, everywhere it shows. Sale, Sold out and New keep the colors of Theme settings. Both filled : the badge takes both colors as they are. Background only : the text is picked for you. It takes the text color or the background color of Scheme 1, your main color scheme, whichever contrasts more with the badge. If even that one stays below a contrast of 4.5:1, which happens on mid tones, the text turns pure black or pure white, one of which always reaches it. Text only : the text color sits on the Custom background of Theme settings. Check that the two contrast enough. Neither : the colors of Theme settings, as on every other product."},{"t":"Badges on the product page","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#badges-product-page","x":"Badges on media , in the Product section settings, shows the badges in the corner of the gallery: Off (the default) or Automatic , the same Sale, Sold out, New and Custom badges as the cards. The Badge block, in the information column, draws the same badges in a row when its Badge type is Automatic (Sale, Sold out, New, Custom) , the default. Its other type, Image , places your own artwork in a corner of the product area. The Spinning badge block turns the custom.badge_label text around a ring, on a corner of the gallery or next to the title, with its own position and size on desktop and on mobile. It has no text field of its own: a product without the metafield shows no ring. See Spinning badge . On the product page, Sale and Sold out follow the selected variant: choosing a variant without a compare-at price removes Sale, choosing a sold out one shows Sold out. When no badge applies, nothing is drawn and no space is left."},{"t":"Choose the badges of each section","p":"Features / Product badges","u":"features.html#badges-per-section","x":"Every section that shows product cards has its own Badges setting: Collection, Search, Featured collection, Product recommendations, Recently viewed, Lookbook, the 404 page, Compare products, the Product tile of Bento and the Complementary products block of the product page. All , the default: every badge that applies. Automatic only : Sale, Sold out and New, as set in Theme settings, Product badges. Custom only : only the product's custom.badge_label metafield. None : no badge in that section. For example, keep All on the collection pages and choose Custom only in Featured collection on the home page, so it shows your Limited edition badges without the Sale ones."},{"t":"Age verifier","p":"Features","u":"features.html#age-verifier","x":"A modal that asks visitors to confirm their age before they browse the store. It shows on every page of the online store, never at checkout, and waits for the page loader to leave first. In Theme settings, Age verifier , check Enable the age verifier . Set the Minimum age . Write [age] in the texts to print it. Fields left empty use the translated storefront text. Choose what happens when the visitor declines: Show a message or Redirect to a link . Set Remember the answer for : the number of days before the same browser is asked again. 0 asks on every visit. Style it with a background image, a color scheme and a card style. Check Preview in the theme editor to see it while you edit; answers are not remembered while previewing. Raising the minimum age asks every visitor again. A decline is never remembered. The age verifier is a self-declaration, not an identity check: make sure it meets the rules that apply to your products in the countries you sell to."},{"t":"Gift wrapping","p":"Features","u":"features.html#gift-wrapping","x":"Adds a gift wrapping checkbox, and an optional gift message, to the cart drawer and the cart page. Checking the box adds your wrapping product to the cart in quantity 1 and records the cart attribute Gift wrapping: Yes . The message is saved as the cart attribute Gift message . Both appear on the order in your admin. Create a product for the wrapping, for example Gift wrapping , with the price the buyer pays and an image. Make it available on the Online Store sales channel, and keep it out of your collections. In Theme settings, Gift wrapping , check Offer gift wrapping and pick it as the Wrapping product . The option only shows once an available product is chosen. Adjust the Checkbox label , the help text, the gift message and its maximum length, and where it shows: cart drawer, cart page or both. The wrapping line stays at quantity 1, and a cart that holds only the wrapping is emptied, so nobody checks out with the wrapping alone."},{"t":"Lookbook","p":"Features","u":"features.html#lookbook","x":"The Lookbook section turns a photo into a shop: each point on the image opens the product card, with its quick add. On a phone a tap opens the same content as a sheet from the bottom of the screen. Add a Lookbook section and choose an image, plus an optional mobile image. Add one Hotspot block per product and pick the product. A hotspot can carry a text and a link instead. Place each hotspot with Horizontal position and Vertical position , in percent of the image: 0% is the left or top edge, 100% the right or bottom edge. Desktop and mobile positions are separate. For a shoppable list, set Layout to Image with product list : the products line up beside the image, and hovering a card lights its hotspot."},{"t":"Compare products","p":"Features","u":"features.html#compare-products","x":"The Compare products section sets up to five products side by side. Built in rows show the image, the badges, the price, the availability, the vendor and the rating. Each row you add reads one fact on every compared product: a metafield of your choice, or the vendor, product type, tags, SKU, barcode, weight or unit price. Create one product metafield definition per fact you want to compare, in Settings, Custom data, Products. For example Texture and Skin type (Single line text), Fragrance free (True or false). Fill the values on each product. Add the section, pick the products, then add one Row block per fact. Keep Source on Metafield and type the metafield's name in Metafield , for example Skin type , or its key, custom.skin_type . Type a Label for the left column, or leave it empty to use the name of the source. Each value is drawn by its type: a check mark or a cross for true or false, a number followed by the row's Unit , a list as a sentence, a color with its swatch. A product without a value shows a hyphen. Highlight differences marks the rows where products differ. Mobile layout shows one card per product on a phone, or the table with the labels in place while the products s"},{"t":"Recently viewed","p":"Features","u":"features.html#recently-viewed","x":"The product page records each product a visitor opens, in that visitor's own browser. The Recently viewed section reads that list and shows the products, newest first. Nothing is sent to a server and no app or account is needed. The section takes no space until the visitor has a history; in the theme editor it shows example cards instead. Add it to the product template, below Product recommendations, with Exclude the current product on, or to the cart, collection or home page. Maximum products caps the list."},{"t":"Pagination","p":"Features","u":"features.html#pagination","x":"The Collection and Search sections have a Pagination setting with three modes: Page numbers : classic numbered pages. Load more button : the next page is added under the grid when the shopper asks for it. Infinite scroll : the next page is added as the shopper reaches the end of the grid. After three pages a Load more button takes over, so the footer stays reachable. Load more and infinite scroll show a Showing X of Y counter. The number of products per page is set with Products per page on collections and Results per page on search. The blog, the list of collections and blog post comments use page numbers, with their own per page setting. Promo tiles appear on the first page only."},{"t":"Translations","p":"Features","u":"features.html#translations","x":"Balm Studio ships in five languages: English, French, German, Italian and Spanish. That covers every storefront text of the theme (buttons, cart, forms, filters, accessibility labels) and the theme editor itself, which follows the language of your admin. Add and publish your languages in Settings, Languages . The theme's own texts switch automatically. Translate the content you typed in the editor (headings, paragraphs, button labels) with Shopify's free Translate & Adapt app. Leave the text settings marked Leave empty to use the translated default empty on a multilingual store: they then show the built in text in each language. To change the wording of a theme text, use Edit default theme content in the theme's ... menu in your theme library. For a language Balm Studio does not ship, Translate & Adapt can translate the theme texts too."},{"t":"Combined listings","p":"Features","u":"features.html#combined-listings","x":"Combined listings group separate products into one listing, for example one product per color, and are available to Shopify Plus stores through Shopify's Combined Listings app. Balm Studio supports them with nothing to configure: On the product page, picking a value that belongs to another product of the listing switches the page to that product without a reload, keeping the values already chosen and updating the address. Swatches on product cards link to the matching product. In quick view, a value from another product loads that product into the modal. In the quick add option picker, such a value opens that product's page, where the full picker takes over."},{"t":"Pre-order","p":"Features","u":"features.html#pre-order","x":"Pre-order turns itself on: there is nothing to enable. A variant becomes a pre-order when its quantity is tracked, its stock is at 0 and Continue selling when out of stock is checked in the product admin. The add to cart button, the sticky add to cart bar and the quick add button then read Pre-order , or the Button label you set in Theme settings, Pre-order . The variant can still be bought, so the accelerated checkout buttons (Buy it now) stay visible, unlike on a sold out variant. The Stock status block keeps its own text. The label does not change how checkout works: the order is paid at checkout like any other. To take a deposit or charge later, use a pre-order app that creates selling plans; its options then show in the Purchase options block. Tell buyers when the product will ship, for example in a Text block or a Collapsible row."},{"t":"Type sizes","p":"Features","u":"features.html#type-sizes","x":"Every text of Balm Studio sits on one fluid type scale, from phones to large screens. A size is reached at 390 px wide for its mobile value and at 1440 px for its desktop value, and grows in a straight line in between, so a heading never jumps from one size to another as the window widens. The text size settings of the sections and blocks follow the same rule, and their defaults sit on the scale: a section you add matches its neighbors without any tuning. To make the whole store read larger or smaller, move Heading scale or Body scale in Theme settings, Typography (80 to 130%). They multiply every size, those set in sections included, so the proportions between levels stay. To change one element, use its own size settings: they stay on the fluid rule and the scales still apply to them. Product card titles and prices are set once for all the grids in Theme settings, Product cards . The announcement bar and the mega menu switch their sizes at 1200 px, the menu breakpoint. Logos and decorative texts are sized on their own, off the scale: the Large logo of the footer fills its width, and the text behind cutouts of the product page or the two words across the Gallery banner keep a deskt"},{"t":"Page width","p":"Features","u":"features.html#page-width","x":"One setting, Page width in Theme settings, Layout , sets how wide the shopping pages grow: the product page, the collection and search pages, and the Featured collection, Product recommendations and Recently viewed sections. Standard keeps them to 1400 px, Wide to 1600 px, and Full width with margins fills the screen less the side margins of the header, so the page, the breadcrumbs and the footer line up with the header's logo and icons. On a large screen, Wide shows bigger product cards and a bigger gallery; the card images are served at the new size, so they stay sharp. The other sections set their width with Section width , whose default, Theme default, follows Default section width in the same Layout group."},{"t":"Automatic header colors","p":"Features","u":"features.html#header-colors","x":"The header can lie over the top of the page, transparent, and wear the colors that read on what is under it, with nothing to set in each section. It does so with Header behavior on Transparent at top (the default: over the first section, then the card on scroll) or Adaptive (at every scroll position, on every page). In the Header section, set Colors over dark backgrounds to a color scheme with light text. Scheme 2 of the Balm Studio preset, white on near black, is the default. Upload a light version of your logo in Logo for dark backgrounds . It shares the size and the place of the main logo, so nothing moves when they swap. Let the first section of the page reach under the header: Allow transparent header on a Hero, Slideshow, Video, Products showcase or Brand story hero, or Header over this section on the other sections that offer it (see The header over a section ). The header then reads the backgrounds painted under its middle line: colors, gradients, each product's gradient, and, over a picture or a video, a small thumbnail of the part it covers, overlay included. Over a dark background it takes the colors over dark backgrounds and the logo for dark backgrounds; over a light o"},{"t":"Section width","p":"Features","u":"features.html#section-width","x":"Almost every section has a Section width setting, right after its color scheme, with four options: Theme default , the default: the Default section width of Theme settings, Layout (Full width with margins unless you change it), so every section left on it changes width at once. Full width : the background, the picture or the video runs from one edge of the screen to the other, with square corners. Text keeps a readable width inside. Full width with margins : the section stops at the Section side margins of Theme settings, Layout, one value on desktop and one on mobile. Page width : the section stops at the Page width of Theme settings, Layout, with its side margin, in line with the product, collection and search pages. Mixing the options on one page builds a rhythm: a Full width hero, products and texts at Page width, then a picture in Full width with margins with rounded corners. Inset, Before and after and the Slideshow take a Corner radius of their own, the media radius of the theme by default. Product, Contact and Collection keep their background edge to edge in every width, for a transparent header, and move only their content. See Sections, Section width ."},{"t":"Social media","p":"Features","u":"features.html#social-media","x":"Your social media profiles are typed once, in Theme settings, Social media , and every icon of the store reads them. In Theme settings, Social media, paste the full address of each profile you have, for example https://www.tiktok.com/@yourbrand . Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, X, YouTube, Pinterest, Snapchat, Threads, Tumblr, Vimeo and LinkedIn are offered. Choose where the icons appear: the Social media links block of the footer, the Social media links section, and the header on desktop with Show social media icons in the Header section. Only the networks with an address show, each with its icon, in a new tab. Screen readers name each link after your store, such as Balm on Instagram . The footer block can also show Shopify's Follow on Shop button. How your pages look when someone shares them is set separately, in Social media sharing ."},{"t":"Sticky add to cart","p":"Features","u":"features.html#sticky-add-to-cart","x":"A bar that keeps the product and its add to cart button within reach while the shopper scrolls a long product page. It is the Sticky add to cart section, which the product template places below the Product section. Enable the bar turns it on. Position (desktop) and Position (mobile) put it at the top or at the bottom of the screen; the bottom suits phones, where the main button quickly scrolls away. It shows the Product thumbnail (desktop and mobile apart), the Product title , the Selected variant (left out on a product without variants) and the Price , each one optional. By default it appears once the main buy button scrolls out of view; Always visible keeps it on screen. The button follows the variant chosen on the page and says Pre-order on a pre-order variant. Its colors are Button background and Button text ; with the Product gradient background, the product's end color becomes its accent when it stays readable. The back to top button lifts above the bar. In the theme editor, the bar steps aside while another section is selected."},{"t":"Column selector","p":"Features","u":"features.html#collection-columns","x":"The Collection section can let shoppers choose how many products they see per row. Columns (desktop) and Columns (mobile) set the starting layout; then: Let visitors change the column count (desktop) adds 2, 3 and 4 buttons beside the sort. Let visitors change the column count (mobile) adds 1 and 2 buttons beside the filters on phones. On desktop the buttons sit on one row with the filters, the product count and the sort; on a phone, on one row with the Filter and sort button and the count. Each device keeps its own choice for the rest of the visit, after a filter or a page reload too. Both are off by default."},{"t":"Metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html","x":"Metafields give every product its own color, cutout, texts and images. This page lists the metafields Balm Studio reads, with the exact name, key and type to create."},{"t":"Before you start","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#before-you-start","x":"The theme cannot create a metafield definition; only you can, in your admin. This is a platform rule: a setting can only be connected to a definition that already exists, with the right type. So the definition always comes first, the connection second, the values third. Definitions are created in Settings, Custom data , under Products , Collections , Pages or Shop , depending on what carries the value. Type the Name exactly as listed below. The admin derives the key from the name, in lowercase with underscores, so the key matches on its own. If you rename a definition, check its key before saving: the connection works by key. Names are shown in quotation marks here and in the theme editor so you can see where they start and end. The quotation marks are not part of the name. The namespace and key are suggestions; the type is not. A setting refuses a definition of the wrong type. Every connectable setting repeats the definition it expects in its own help text in the editor."},{"t":"Product color","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#product-color","x":"Balm Studio dresses every page in the color of the product it shows. Each product needs two colors, a dark one and a light one; the theme works out the grounds and the texts of the page from them and checks their contrast. The theme reads these keys directly: create the definitions once, then fill the values on each product. There is nothing to connect in the theme editor. The same two colors can be set on a variant ( custom.background_color , custom.background_color_end and custom.cutout , under Settings, Custom data, Variants ): choosing that variant on the product page recolors the page. A variant without them uses the color of its swatch, then the product's. On a collection , the same two color keys (under Settings, Custom data, Collections ) give the collection page its color; without them, the color of the first product. In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name Background color , namespace and key custom.background_color , type Color . Save. Repeat with Background color end ( custom.background_color_end , Color ), Cutout ( custom.cutout , File , images only), Name lines ( custom.name_lines , Single line text ), Volume ( custom.volume , Single line tex"},{"t":"Product texts","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#product-texts","x":"The product passport (the Specification rows of the product page) and the Texture section print texts you connect to metafields of your choice, so that every product says its own. Create the definitions first: Shopify refuses to save a template connected to a definition that does not exist yet. Suggested definitions, all on products: To connect one, select the setting in the theme editor, choose the dynamic source icon next to it and pick the metafield. A row or a text whose metafield is empty on a product is not printed."},{"t":"Article product","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#article-product","x":"A blog article metafield, Product ( custom.product , type Product , one value, under Settings, Custom data, Blog posts ), links an article to one product. The Journal and Journal article sections then paint the article in that product's color and show the product at the end of the article. Without it, the article uses the house pair."},{"t":"Metaobjects","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#metaobjects","x":"Balm Studio reads no metaobject: there is nothing to create under Settings, Custom data, Metaobject definitions . The Ingredient atlas is built from its own Ingredient blocks, each with a name, a note and the products that contain it."},{"t":"Metafields the theme reads directly","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#read-directly","x":"These keys need a definition and a value, and nothing else: the theme reads them by key, so there is nothing to connect in the theme editor. Create each definition once, with exactly this namespace and key, then fill the value on each product, in the Metafields card of the product page in your admin. Compare products reads no fixed key: each of its rows reads the metafield you name. See Compare products rows ."},{"t":"Badge label, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#badge-label","x":"In your admin, open Settings , then Custom data , then Products . Choose Add definition . Name: Badge label . Check that the namespace and key read custom.badge_label . Select the type Single line text (under Text), keep One value , and save. Open a product, find the Metafields card, type the badge text in Badge label , for example Limited edition , and save. The badge now shows wherever that product appears as a card, in quick view and in Compare products. On the product page it shows when Badges on media is on Automatic or a Badge block is in the column. Its colors are in Theme settings, Product badges , unless the product has its own (below). Clear the value and the badge goes."},{"t":"Badge colors, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#badge-colors","x":"Optional: only for products whose Custom badge should not wear the colors of Theme settings. In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name: Badge color , namespace and key custom.badge_color , type Color . Save. Choose Add definition again. Name: Badge text color , namespace and key custom.badge_text_color , type Color . Save. Open a product that has a Badge label , and in its Metafields card pick a Badge color , for example a deep green. Pick a Badge text color too, or leave it empty. With only the badge color, the text is picked for you: the text color or the background color of Scheme 1, whichever contrasts more with the badge, or pure black or white when neither reaches 4.5:1. With only the text color, the text sits on the Custom background of Theme settings. Create both as Color : a value that is not a color, such as a word typed in a text metafield, is ignored. The two colors apply to the Custom badge only, never to Sale, Sold out or New, and not to the Spinning badge, which keeps the colors set in its block."},{"t":"Primary collection, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#primary-collection","x":"Optional: for products that sit in several collections, to choose the one the breadcrumb trail shows. In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name: Primary collection , namespace and key custom.primary_collection , type Collection (under References), one value. Save. Open a product, and in its Metafields card pick the collection in Primary collection . Check that Show breadcrumbs and Show the collection are on in Theme settings, Breadcrumbs . A visitor who arrives from a collection grid still sees that collection in the trail; the metafield decides for the others, such as a visitor coming from a search engine. Search engines read the same trail."},{"t":"Banner image, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#banner-image","x":"Optional: for collections whose banner needs another picture than the collection image, or a precise framing. In Settings, Custom data, Collections , choose Add definition . Name: Banner image , namespace and key custom.banner_image , type File , with images accepted. Save. Open a collection in Products, Collections , and in its Metafields card pick the picture. To control the framing, set the focal point of the picture in Content, Files . The banner takes, in this order, this metafield, the Banner image of the Collection section, then the collection's own image. Shopify keeps no focal point on a collection's own image, which is why the metafield and the section setting exist."},{"t":"Page image, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#page-image","x":"Optional: for pages linked from the main menu, so their link shows a picture in the dropdowns and in Image cards. In Settings, Custom data, Pages , choose Add definition . Name: Image , namespace and key custom.image , type File , with images accepted. Save. Open a page in Online Store, Pages , and pick its picture in the Metafields card. A page without it shows its link without a picture, and an Image cards block set to Automatic leaves it out."},{"t":"Tagline, step by step","p":"Metafields / Metafields the theme reads directly","u":"metafields.html#tagline","x":"In Settings, Custom data, Products , choose Add definition . Name: Tagline , namespace and key custom.tagline , type Single line text . Save. Fill it on each product, for example Rich overnight repair for dry skin . The default product template already has a Text block with Source set to Tagline under the title. On another template, add a Text block and choose that source. A product without a tagline shows nothing there, not even the space of the line. In the theme editor, a dimmed example stands in so you can place and size the block."},{"t":"Product metafields you connect","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#product-metafields","x":"Create these in Settings, Custom data, Products , then connect them with the dynamic source icon next to the setting. The names and keys are suggestions; only the type matters."},{"t":"Icon metafields, step by step","p":"Metafields / Product metafields you connect","u":"metafields.html#icon-metafields","x":"The Icon list of the product page holds up to three claims, each an Icon item block, and each claim can come from the product: an icon picture and a line of text per item, numbered by item. Create the ones you need: In Settings, Custom data, Products , add the definitions: for example Icon image 1 , type File , and Icon text 1 , type Multi-line text (or Single line text for one line). Fill them on each product, for example a leaf picture and Vegan formula . In the theme editor, open a product, select the first Icon item of the Icon list, then next to Icon image select the dynamic source icon and pick Icon image 1 . Do the same next to Heading with Icon text 1 . Repeat for the second and third items. These names and keys are suggestions: any key works, as long as the type matches, since you connect them yourself. An item whose heading and text both come back empty stays hidden on the storefront and leaves no gap; in the theme editor it keeps a small badge that says why."},{"t":"Metafields you type by key","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#typed-keys","x":"A few settings are plain text fields where you type the namespace.key yourself instead of using the dynamic source icon."},{"t":"Product list metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#product-lists","x":"The Products setting of the Product upsell block, of the Complementary products block and of the cart drawer suggestions can be connected to a product metafield of type Product , set to accept a list of products. Each product then carries its own hand picked selection, for example Upsell products with the key custom.upsell_products . The block's Products come from setting must be on A manual selection ."},{"t":"Shop metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#shop-metafields","x":"Every other section that paints a background (rich text, featured collection, FAQ, contact, image with text and so on) offers the same Section background settings. Those sections are not tied to a product, so their colors connect to shop metafields, created in Settings, Custom data, Shop . One value then applies storewide, which lets you restyle every connected section at once."},{"t":"Review metafields","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#reviews","x":"The Rating block, the ratings on product cards, in quick view and in Compare products read Shopify's standard review metafields, reviews.rating (Rating) and reviews.rating_count (Integer). Review apps fill them; you have nothing to create. Until they are filled, the ratings stay hidden."},{"t":"Compare products rows","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#compare","x":"Compare products has no metafield of its own. Each Row block with Source set to Metafield reads the product metafield you name in its Metafield setting, on every compared product, so you decide which facts the table compares. Type the metafield's name, exactly as it shows in Settings, Custom data, Products ( Skin type ), or its key ( custom.skin_type ). A name is turned into the key the admin gives it by default: namespace custom , the name in lowercase with underscores. If you changed the key of a definition, type the key. The field takes no dynamic source on purpose: a connected metafield would give the value of the page's product in every column. To name the row after the metafield, connect it to the row's Label instead, or leave Label empty to show the name you typed. For example, to compare three creams of a range: Create one definition per fact, as in the table. These names and keys are examples: any name works, as long as the row names the same metafield. Fill the values on each product you compare, in the Metafields card of the product. In the theme editor, open the Compare products section and add one Row block per fact. Keep Source on Metafield, type the name or the key i"},{"t":"What happens on a product with no value","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#empty-values","x":"Nothing breaks and nothing goes blank, which is what lets you fill only the products you care about. A background color that comes back empty falls through, in this order: the Fallback background color setting, if you set one; otherwise the background of the section's color scheme. In a Products showcase spotlight and in Featured set, the order is the override field, then the product's metafield, then the background of the section's color scheme. In the Product gradient mode of the product page, one color alone paints a flat background and no color leaves the color scheme; the fallback color is not used there. For the Custom badge, an empty custom.badge_color or custom.badge_text_color leaves the Custom colors of Theme settings. Behind cutout images, an empty tagline shows no text, and an empty custom.background_color_end gives the text the scheme text color. Never connect the fallback color itself to a metafield: it is the safety net. If one end of a gradient is empty, the other end fills the whole wash; if a halo color is empty, the halo is not drawn and the base color stays. An empty text, rich text or image metafield shows nothing on the storefront: never an example text, never"},{"t":"Settings that cannot be connected","p":"Metafields","u":"metafields.html#not-connectable","x":"Shopify only allows connections on colors, text, rich text, images, videos, links, pages, collections, products and metaobjects. Sliders, checkboxes, dropdowns, the color scheme and Liquid code are fixed for the whole template. When one product needs a different value for one of those, give it a second product template ."},{"t":"Custom code","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html","x":"Balm Studio is built to be shaped from the theme editor, without code. If you or a developer do edit the theme code, read this page first."},{"t":"Get help from a Shopify Partner","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#hire-a-partner","x":"Code customizations are outside the scope of Balm Studio support. For custom features, design changes or integrations, we recommend working with a Shopify Partner: developers and agencies vetted by Shopify, listed in the Shopify Partner Directory ."},{"t":"Try the editor first","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#before-coding","x":"Many changes need no edit to the theme files: The Custom Liquid section, and the Liquid blocks of the product page and of the content sections, accept your own Liquid, HTML and app snippets. Shopify's Custom CSS field, at the bottom of each section's settings and in Theme settings, takes CSS scoped to that section or to the whole store. The Apps section and app blocks place app content without touching the code. Code added this way is kept when you update the theme."},{"t":"Theme updates and your code","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#updates-and-code","x":"When you update Balm Studio, Shopify installs the new version as a separate copy and carries over your theme editor settings and content, but not the changes you made in the theme files. Keep a list of every file you changed and why, so the changes can be applied again to the new version."},{"t":"What support covers","p":"Custom code","u":"custom-code.html#support-scope","x":"Balm Studio support covers the theme as shipped. When a problem shows up on a theme whose code was modified, we may ask you to reproduce it on an unmodified copy of Balm Studio first. See Support ."},{"t":"FAQ","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html","x":"Answers to the questions merchants ask most about Balm Studio."},{"t":"Can I use Balm Studio on more than one store?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#can-i-use-balm-studio-on-more-than-one-store","x":"A theme bought from the Shopify Theme Store is licensed for one store. To use Balm Studio on another store, buy it again from that store. Trying the theme is free on any store."},{"t":"How do I update Balm Studio without losing my settings?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-update-balm-studio-without-losing-my-settings","x":"When an update is available, your theme library shows a notice. Shopify adds the new version as a separate copy that keeps your theme editor settings and content. Preview it, then publish it. Changes you made in the theme code are not carried over; see Custom code ."},{"t":"How do I make the header transparent over my hero?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-make-the-header-transparent-over-my-hero","x":"In the Header section, keep Header behavior on Transparent at top , the default, or choose Adaptive . Make sure the first section of the page is a Hero, Slideshow, Video, Products showcase or Brand story hero with Allow transparent header checked, or another section with Header over this section checked. If your hero is dark, upload a light version of your logo in Logo for dark backgrounds , and check that Colors over dark backgrounds is a scheme with light text. The header picks them on its own over a dark image. A floating announcement bar over the same image can follow those colors: check Use the header's colors over dark backgrounds in the Announcement bar section. See the white header example . On the product page, the Product section can run its Product gradient under the transparent header: see Extend the gradient under the header ."},{"t":"Why does the product gradient not reach under the header?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-the-product-gradient-not-reach-under-the-header","x":"Four conditions, all needed: Background mode of the Product section is Product gradient (metafields) , Extend the background under the header is checked, the Header section has Header behavior on Transparent at top or Adaptive, and the Product section is the first section of the product template. A Solid announcement bar in full width stays above the gradient; a Floating or Glass bar lets it run underneath. The header picks light or dark colors for each product on its own: if its text is hard to read over a dark gradient, check that Colors over dark backgrounds in the Header is a scheme with light text. See Extend the gradient under the header ."},{"t":"Why is there no country or language selector in my header?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-is-there-no-country-or-language-selector-in-my-header","x":"The selectors only show when there is a choice to make. The country selector needs at least two countries or regions in Settings, Markets ; the language selector needs at least two published languages in Settings, Languages , active in the visitor's market. Then check that Country and language selectors in the Header section is not set to Off. See Country and language selectors ."},{"t":"Why are there no filters on my collection pages?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-are-there-no-filters-on-my-collection-pages","x":"Filters come from Shopify's free Search & Discovery app. Install it, add the filters you want (availability, price, product type, color and so on), then check that Enable filters is on in the Collection and Search sections. A filter only shows when the products of the page have values for it."},{"t":"How do I set up a mega menu?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-set-up-a-mega-menu","x":"Create your main menu in your admin first. Then, in the Header section, add a Mega menu block and type the exact title of a top level menu item in Linked menu item , for example Shop . Pick a Layout : Links and images builds the panel from that item's sub-links on its own; Custom blocks uses the Link column, Image, Image cards, Products, Promo or Banner blocks you add inside it. The panel opens when a shopper hovers that item. See Mega menu blocks ."},{"t":"How do I give each product its own background color?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-give-each-product-its-own-background-color","x":"Create two product metafield definitions of type Color, Background color ( custom.background_color ) and Background color end ( custom.background_color_end ), and fill them on each product. Then set Background mode of the Product section to Product gradient (metafields) : there is nothing to connect, and one color alone gives a flat background. For a solid color or a radial halo, connect the metafield to the setting instead. Both ways are on Metafields ."},{"t":"How do I make all headings, or all text, larger?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-make-all-headings-or-all-text-larger","x":"Use Heading scale and Body scale in Theme settings, Typography. They multiply every size of the theme, the ones set in sections and blocks included, from 80 to 130%. Changing each section's sizes one by one is only worth it for a single element. See Type sizes ."},{"t":"Why is there no text behind my product image?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-is-there-no-text-behind-my-product-image","x":"The text of Text behind cutouts only shows behind PNG and WebP images; JPG images, videos and 3D models never get it. Check that Show on desktop or Show on mobile is on for the device you are looking at, and that the first media of the gallery is a PNG or WebP image when Apply to is First image only. With Text on Product tagline, a product whose custom.tagline is empty shows no text. See Text behind cutout images ."},{"t":"Why does the spinning badge not show on some products?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-the-spinning-badge-not-show-on-some-products","x":"The ring prints the product's custom.badge_label metafield and has no text of its own: a product with no value shows no ring. Fill the metafield on that product (see Badge label, step by step ). With Next to the title , the page also needs a Title block."},{"t":"Where are Balm spotlight, Lifestyle strip, the Sticky add to cart and Quantity blocks?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#where-are-balm-spotlight-lifestyle-strip-the-sticky-add-to-c","x":"They belonged to preview versions of Balm Studio and were removed before release, together with the free text of the spinning badge. Balm spotlight , the second version of the Product section: its gradient and its spinning badge are now the Product gradient background mode and the positions of the Spinning badge block, on the one Product section. Lifestyle strip , two photos side by side: the section has been removed. Sticky add to cart block : the bar is the Sticky add to cart section, placed below the Product section in the product template. Spinning badge text : the ring of the product page reads the product's custom.badge_label metafield only. The spotlights of the Products showcase keep a text of their own: see Spinning badge of a spotlight . Quantity block : the quantity selector is part of the Buy buttons block, set by Quantity selector (desktop) and Quantity selector (mobile) ."},{"t":"Why can I not connect a setting to my metafield?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-can-i-not-connect-a-setting-to-my-metafield","x":"Three usual causes. The definition does not exist yet: create it in Settings, Custom data first. The type does not match: a color setting only accepts a Color metafield, an image setting a File metafield. Or the definition was created for the wrong resource: product page settings need a Products definition, other sections a Shop definition. The help text of each connectable setting names the exact definition it expects."},{"t":"How do I add product reviews and star ratings?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-add-product-reviews-and-star-ratings","x":"Install a reviews app that writes Shopify's standard review metafields (most do). Balm Studio's Rating block, the ratings on product cards and quick view read them automatically once reviews come in. If the app offers an app block for its review list, add it to the product page from the block picker."},{"t":"How do I add a size guide or ingredients list to product pages?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-add-a-size-guide-or-ingredients-list-to-product-pag","x":"Create a page with the content in Online Store, Pages. On the product page, add a Popup block (a link that opens a dialog) or a Collapsible row , and set Content comes from to A page . For content that differs per product, connect the block's Content to a rich text metafield instead."},{"t":"Can I change the color of the Shop Pay or PayPal buttons?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#can-i-change-the-color-of-the-shop-pay-or-paypal-buttons","x":"No theme can. The accelerated checkout buttons are drawn by Shopify with the brand colors of each payment provider. Balm Studio matches everything Shopify allows: height, corner radius, spacing and the loading placeholder. See The accelerated checkout buttons ."},{"t":"How do I show a free shipping progress bar?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-show-a-free-shipping-progress-bar","x":"In Theme settings, Cart , keep Show the free shipping bar checked and type the amount in Free shipping threshold . The bar only displays progress: create the matching free shipping rate or automatic discount in your admin, and keep the two amounts the same, or buyers will be promised something checkout does not apply."},{"t":"Why does the Buy it now button disappear on some variants?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-the-buy-it-now-button-disappear-on-some-variants","x":"The accelerated checkout buttons (Buy it now, Shop Pay, PayPal and the other wallets) are hidden while the selected variant is sold out, since it cannot be bought, and come back when the shopper picks a variant in stock. A variant that sells as a pre-order can be bought, so it keeps them. See The accelerated checkout buttons ."},{"t":"How do I offer pre-orders?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-offer-pre-orders","x":"Set the variant to continue selling when out of stock in the product admin. At 0 stock its buttons read Pre-order, or the label you set in Theme settings, Pre-order. To take a deposit or charge later, use a pre-order app. See Pre-order ."},{"t":"How do I translate my store?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-translate-my-store","x":"Add and publish your languages in Settings, Languages. Balm Studio's own texts are already translated into French, German, Italian and Spanish. Translate what you typed in the editor with the Translate & Adapt app. See Translations ."},{"t":"The newsletter popup does not appear. What should I check?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#the-newsletter-popup-does-not-appear-what-should-i-check","x":"Enable popup is checked in the Newsletter popup section, and the section is on the template you are viewing (by default, the home page only). You closed it earlier: it stays hidden for the number of days in Reappear after . Test in a private window. The Open delay has not passed yet."},{"t":"Why does my header change color as I scroll?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#why-does-my-header-change-color-as-i-scroll","x":"With Header behavior on Transparent at top or Adaptive, the header reads what lies under it and wears the colors that read best there: its own color scheme and logo over a light background, Colors over dark backgrounds and Logo for dark backgrounds over a dark one. With Adaptive it does so at every scroll position, so it changes as dark and light sections pass under it. To keep one look everywhere, set Header behavior to Standard . See Automatic header colors ."},{"t":"How do I line up a section with the header or make it edge to edge?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-line-up-a-section-with-the-header-or-make-it-edge-t","x":"Use the section's Section width setting. Full width runs the background or the picture from one edge of the screen to the other, Full width with margins stops at the Section side margins of Theme settings, Layout, and Page width lines it up with the product and collection pages. Theme default , the default, follows Default section width in Theme settings, Layout: change it there to move every section left on it at once. See Section width ."},{"t":"Where do I add my Instagram, TikTok and other social media links?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#where-do-i-add-my-instagram-tiktok-and-other-social-media-li","x":"In Theme settings, Social media : paste the full address of each profile. The icons then show in the footer's Social media links block and in the Social media links section, and in the header on desktop when Show social media icons is checked. Networks without an address stay hidden. See Social media ."},{"t":"How do I hide the Sale badges in one section only?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-hide-the-sale-badges-in-one-section-only","x":"Set that section's Badges setting to Custom only (only your custom.badge_label badges) or None . The other sections keep their own choice. Every section with product cards has it, as do the Bento Product tile and the Complementary products block. See Choose the badges of each section ."},{"t":"How do I let shoppers choose the number of columns on collection pages?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#how-do-i-let-shoppers-choose-the-number-of-columns-on-collec","x":"In the Collection section, check Let visitors change the column count (desktop) , which adds 2, 3 and 4 buttons beside the sort, and Let visitors change the column count (mobile) , which adds 1 and 2 buttons beside the filters on phones. Each device keeps the shopper's choice for the rest of the visit. See Column selector ."},{"t":"My speed score dropped after I turned on the page loader. Why?","p":"FAQ","u":"faq.html#my-speed-score-dropped-after-i-turned-on-the-page-loader-why","x":"A loader covers the page while it loads, which speed tools measure as a slower page. Set Page loader to First visit only , the recommended setting, or turn it off. Every page shows it on each page view and has the largest effect."},{"t":"Changelog","p":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html","x":"What changed in each version of Balm Studio. The version installed in your store is shown in your theme library, under the theme name."},{"t":"1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","p":"Changelog","u":"changelog.html#v-1-0-0-2026-10-30","x":"Initial release."},{"t":"Design (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-design","x":"Tone on tone: each product carries a tone, two colors stored in the product metafields custom.background_color and custom.background_color_end . The theme derives six colors from them on the server (field, tone, ink, deep, deeptone and paper), checks every text pair for contrast and corrects it before the page is sent, so pages are right and readable without JavaScript. A product page, a collection, the cart and the hero take the tone of what they show, and move smoothly from one tone to the next. Headings in Gloock, body text in Instrument Sans, one easing curve for every movement, square corners, no glass, shadow or faded text. Sliders use the words Previous and Next and a counter (\"02 / 05\") instead of drawn arrows and dots. Filled buttons, underlined links, accordions with a turning \"+\" and underlined fields are shared by the whole theme. Visitors who ask for less motion get every state at once, with nothing moving while they scroll."},{"t":"Preset (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-preset","x":"Balm Studio: a house tone, Gloock and Instrument Sans, the demo store's templates and header and footer groups, with no image, product, collection or metafield of the demo. Sections and blocks added in the theme editor come with example texts that say how to use them, in the language of the theme editor."},{"t":"Theme settings (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-theme-settings","x":"Tone: the house pair of colors, used where no product sets the tone. Colors, Typography and Layout (page width, default section width, side margins). Buttons: Size (Small, Medium, Large), Border width and Font weight, for every button of the theme, filled buttons included. A small button keeps a 44 px tap area. Tiles, Product badges, Pre-order, Quick view, Cart, Gift wrapping, Back to top, Age verifier, Favicon, Social media, Social media sharing, Breadcrumbs, Search and Search engines."},{"t":"Sections (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-sections","x":"Every section has a Surface setting: Field (the page's tone, the default), Deep, Paper, Color scheme or Image. Text on each surface reads at 4.5:1 at least. Home and content: Hero sequence (products that rise and turn as the page scrolls, the page following their tone), Hero, Campaign, Color library, A day in color, Routine builder, Reviews, Atelier, Line-up, Hue finder, Texture, Ingredient atlas, Chapters, Numbers, Scroll-revealed text, Marquee, Rich text (with a Statement style and Product inline blocks that set a small product in the sentence), Image (Reveal on scroll, on by default), Slideshow (a counter on phones from five slides), Featured product, Featured collection, Collection list, Key figures, Key ingredients, FAQ, Contact, Newsletter, Testimonials, Lookbook, Video and more: 74 sections in all. Section width on every section: Page width, Full width with margins or Full width, the background always running edge to edge."},{"t":"Product page (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-product-page","x":"A scene with the product's name in layers behind the product cut out ( custom.cutout , else its photo), a buy column, a passport of the product's facts, a sticky add to cart bar, the media in a band with zoom, video and 3D, and the variant's own tone. Page transitions: from a collection tile to the product page, the name and the product move into place (View Transitions, where the browser supports them)."},{"t":"Collection, search and cart (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-collection-search-and-cart","x":"Collection tiles on the product's field, an Index view in rows, filters and sorting. Search in a full screen field, products before pages and articles. Cart drawer and cart page: a free delivery bar in segments, a suggestion, the order note, discount codes, gift wrapping, an empty bag with its own sentence and link, and a toast when a product is added."},{"t":"Header and menus (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-header-and-menus","x":"The header takes the surface of the section under it, hides going down and comes back going up. Mega menu with custom blocks, a full screen menu sheet on phones."},{"t":"Accessibility and performance (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-accessibility-and-performance","x":"No axe violation (critical, serious or moderate) on the home, product, collection, search, cart, contact, journal, article and about pages; a visible focus everywhere, keyboard access to every control. Lighthouse on the demo store: performance averages of 86 on mobile and 99 on desktop, accessibility 100."},{"t":"Languages (1.0.0 (2026-10-30))","p":"Changelog / 1.0.0 (2026-10-30)","u":"changelog.html#v-languages","x":"English, French, German, Italian and Spanish, for the storefront and the theme editor."},{"t":"Support","p":"Support","u":"support.html","x":"Balm Studio support answers questions about the theme and fixes its bugs. Here is what it covers and how to reach it."},{"t":"What support covers","p":"Support","u":"support.html#covered","x":"Bugs in the theme as shipped: something that does not work as this documentation describes. Questions about the theme: installing it, its settings, sections, blocks and features, and how to reach a result with them."},{"t":"What support does not cover","p":"Support","u":"support.html#not-covered","x":"Customizations : changes to the theme code, new features, custom designs, or code added in Custom Liquid sections, Liquid blocks or Custom CSS. For this work we recommend a Shopify Partner . Problems caused by edits to the theme files. We may ask you to reproduce the problem on an unmodified copy of Balm Studio. Third party apps and services, and Shopify features outside the theme (checkout, payments, shipping rules, domains). For those, contact the app developer or Shopify Support."},{"t":"Response time","p":"Support","u":"support.html#response-time","x":"We reply within two business days (Monday to Friday), usually sooner."},{"t":"How to send a request","p":"Support","u":"support.html#request","x":"Use the support form . To help us answer in one go, include: your store address ( yourstore.myshopify.com ) and the name of the theme in your library; the link of the page where the problem happens; what you did, what you expected and what happened instead, with a screenshot or a short video if you can; the browser and device you used; whether the theme code was modified. Before writing, it is worth checking the FAQ and searching this documentation. If an app could be involved, try with it turned off."}];
